WEBVTT

00:02:43.512 --> 00:02:46.242
<i>The hills are alive</i>

00:02:46.549 --> 00:02:50.918
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:02:51.187 --> 00:02:53.621
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

00:02:53.923 --> 00:02:58.758
<i>For a thousand years</i>

00:02:59.028 --> 00:03:02.191
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

00:03:02.431 --> 00:03:06.959
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:03:07.236 --> 00:03:14.404
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:19.779
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:23.109
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:27.619
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:31.826
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

00:03:32.094 --> 00:03:35.586
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

00:03:35.831 --> 00:03:39.323
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

00:03:39.602 --> 00:03:43.470
<i>To sing through the night</i>

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:47.505
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

00:03:47.843 --> 00:03:53.475
<i>I go to the hills</i>

00:03:53.682 --> 00:03:59.848
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

00:04:00.122 --> 00:04:03.990
<i>I know I will hear</i>

00:04:04.193 --> 00:04:08.687
<i>What I've heard before</i>

00:04:08.964 --> 00:04:13.697
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

00:04:13.936 --> 00:04:21.707
<i>With the sound of music</i>

00:04:22.778 --> 00:04:27.943
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:37.115
<i>...once more</i>

00:09:19.174 --> 00:09:24.134
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:24.413 --> 00:09:29.077
<i>Hallelujah, hallelujah</i>

00:09:31.286 --> 00:09:33.345
- Reverend Mother.
- Sister Bernice.

00:09:33.589 --> 00:09:36.217
- I simply cannot find her.
- Maria?

00:09:37.292 --> 00:09:38.589
She's missing again.

00:09:39.528 --> 00:09:41.894
We should've put a cowbell
around her neck.

00:09:42.131 --> 00:09:45.191
Have you tried the barn? You know
how much she adores the animals.

00:09:45.467 --> 00:09:48.197
I have looked everywhere.
In all of the usual places.

00:09:48.403 --> 00:09:50.633
Sister, considering it's Maria...

00:09:50.939 --> 00:09:53.533
...I suggest you look in someplace
unusual.

00:09:58.814 --> 00:10:00.111
Well, Reverend Mother...

00:10:00.382 --> 00:10:02.942
...I hope this new infraction ends
whatever doubts...

00:10:03.218 --> 00:10:06.449
...you may still have
about Maria's future here.

00:10:06.655 --> 00:10:10.716
I always try to keep faith
in my doubts, Sister Berthe.

00:10:10.959 --> 00:10:13.826
After all, the wool of a black sheep
is just as warm.

00:10:14.062 --> 00:10:18.396
We are not talking about sheep,
black or white, Sister Margaretta.

00:10:18.634 --> 00:10:22.070
Of all the candidates for
the novitiate, Maria is the least...

00:10:22.337 --> 00:10:24.828
Children, children.

00:10:25.307 --> 00:10:29.266
We were speculating about
the qualifications of our postulants.

00:10:29.912 --> 00:10:32.904
The Mistress of Novices
and the Mistress of Postulants...

00:10:33.148 --> 00:10:38.450
...were trying to help me
by expressing opposite points of view.

00:10:38.687 --> 00:10:41.747
Tell me, Sister Catherine,
what do you think of Maria?

00:10:41.957 --> 00:10:45.017
She's a wonderful girl,
some of the time.

00:10:45.994 --> 00:10:49.088
- Sister Agatha?
- It's very easy to like Maria...

00:10:49.331 --> 00:10:51.856
...except when it's difficult.

00:10:52.167 --> 00:10:55.728
- And you, Sister Sophia?
- Oh, I love her very dearly.

00:10:55.938 --> 00:10:58.873
But she always seems to be
in trouble, doesn't she?

00:10:59.107 --> 00:11:00.699
Exactly what I say.

00:11:01.176 --> 00:11:03.644
<i>She climbs a tree and scrapes her knee</i>

00:11:03.846 --> 00:11:05.541
<i>Her dress has got a tear</i>

00:11:06.215 --> 00:11:10.379
<i>She waltzes on her way to Mass</i>
<i>And whistles on the stair</i>

00:11:11.019 --> 00:11:15.513
<i>And underneath her wimple</i>
<i>She has curlers in her hair</i>

00:11:15.791 --> 00:11:20.387
<i>I've even heard her singing</i>
<i>In the abbey</i>

00:11:20.629 --> 00:11:22.620
<i>She's always late for chapel</i>

00:11:22.865 --> 00:11:25.129
<i>But her penitence is real</i>

00:11:25.400 --> 00:11:27.732
<i>She's always late for everything</i>

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:29.995
<i>Except for every meal</i>

00:11:30.372 --> 00:11:35.071
<i>I hate to have to say it</i>
<i>But I very firmly feel</i>

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:39.747
<i>Maria's not an asset to the abbey</i>

00:11:40.249 --> 00:11:42.740
<i>I'd like to say a word in her behalf</i>

00:11:43.018 --> 00:11:44.349
Say it, Sister Margaretta.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.179
<i>Maria makes me laugh</i>

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:55.996
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:11:56.265 --> 00:12:00.065
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:12:00.369 --> 00:12:03.702
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:12:04.239 --> 00:12:05.331
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

00:12:05.574 --> 00:12:06.905
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>- A clown</i>

00:12:08.543 --> 00:12:12.274
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:12:12.547 --> 00:12:16.005
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:12:16.418 --> 00:12:20.115
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

00:12:20.689 --> 00:12:24.181
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:12:24.426 --> 00:12:28.522
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:12:29.031 --> 00:12:34.560
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:12:34.770 --> 00:12:40.231
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:12:41.310 --> 00:12:44.802
<i>When I'm with her I'm confused</i>
<i>Out of focus and bemused</i>

00:12:45.113 --> 00:12:48.549
<i>And I never know exactly where I am</i>

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:52.083
<i>- Unpredictable as weather</i>
<i>- She's as flighty as a feather</i>

00:12:52.454 --> 00:12:54.285
<i>- She's a darling</i>
<i>- She's a demon</i>

00:12:54.489 --> 00:12:55.820
<i>She's a lamb</i>

00:12:56.224 --> 00:12:59.887
<i>She'll out pester any pest</i>
<i>Drive a hornet from its nest</i>

00:13:00.095 --> 00:13:03.394
<i>She can throw a whirling dervish</i>
<i>Out of whirl</i>

00:13:03.966 --> 00:13:07.493
<i>- She is gentle, she is wild</i>
<i>- She's a riddle, she's a child</i>

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:10.630
<i>- She's a headache</i>
<i>- She's an angel</i>

00:13:10.839 --> 00:13:14.741
<i>She's a girl</i>

00:13:15.477 --> 00:13:19.413
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:13:19.648 --> 00:13:23.345
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

00:13:23.652 --> 00:13:27.144
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

00:13:27.422 --> 00:13:29.413
<i>- A flibbertigibbet</i>
<i>- A will-o'-the-wisp</i>

00:13:29.658 --> 00:13:31.285
<i>A clown</i>

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:35.491
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

00:13:35.764 --> 00:13:39.256
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

00:13:39.468 --> 00:13:43.802
<i>- But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>- And listen to all you say?</i>

00:13:44.039 --> 00:13:48.135
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

00:13:48.343 --> 00:13:54.179
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

00:14:10.132 --> 00:14:16.901
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam...</i>

00:14:17.806 --> 00:14:24.211
<i>...in your hand?</i>

00:14:36.024 --> 00:14:38.015
You may go in now, Maria.

00:14:50.605 --> 00:14:52.232
Come here, my child.

00:14:58.747 --> 00:15:00.112
Now sit down.

00:15:01.049 --> 00:15:04.610
Reverend Mother, I'm sorry.
I couldn't help myself.

00:15:04.886 --> 00:15:07.855
- The hills were beckoning and before...
- Dear.

00:15:08.256 --> 00:15:10.224
I haven't summoned you for apologies.

00:15:10.459 --> 00:15:12.689
Please let me ask for forgiveness.

00:15:13.361 --> 00:15:14.589
If you'll feel better.

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.896
Yes, you see,
the sky was so blue today...

00:15:18.133 --> 00:15:21.933
...and everything was so green and
fragrant, I had to be a part of it.

00:15:22.204 --> 00:15:26.698
The Untersberg led me higher like
it wanted me to go through the clouds.

00:15:26.908 --> 00:15:28.933
Suppose darkness had come
and you were lost?

00:15:29.211 --> 00:15:31.441
Mother, I could never be lost
up there.

00:15:31.713 --> 00:15:34.546
That's my mountain.
I was brought up on it.

00:15:34.749 --> 00:15:37.047
It was the mountain that led me
to you.

00:15:37.819 --> 00:15:40.788
When I was a child,
I would come down and climb a tree...

00:15:41.056 --> 00:15:42.819
...and look in your garden.

00:15:43.058 --> 00:15:45.993
I'd see the sisters at work
and hear them sing.

00:15:47.329 --> 00:15:50.958
Which brings me to another
transgression, Reverend Mother.

00:15:51.166 --> 00:15:53.327
I was singing out there today.

00:15:54.002 --> 00:15:58.029
Only in the abbey do we have rules
about postulants singing.

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.265
I can't stop wherever I am.

00:16:00.475 --> 00:16:02.807
Worse, I can't seem to stop
saying things.

00:16:03.078 --> 00:16:05.342
Everything I think and feel.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:07.013
Some call that "honesty."

00:16:07.282 --> 00:16:09.648
Oh, but it's terrible,
Reverend Mother!

00:16:09.851 --> 00:16:13.753
You know how Sister Berthe makes me
kiss the floor after a disagreement?

00:16:14.122 --> 00:16:17.614
Lately, I kiss the floor
when I see her coming to save time.

00:16:20.295 --> 00:16:21.455
Maria...

00:16:22.464 --> 00:16:25.456
...when you saw us over the wall
and longed to be with us...

00:16:25.700 --> 00:16:30.433
...that didn't mean you were prepared
for the way we live here, did it?

00:16:31.773 --> 00:16:34.173
No, Mother, but I pray and I try.

00:16:34.376 --> 00:16:36.105
And I am learning. I really am.

00:16:36.344 --> 00:16:39.006
What is the most important lesson
you have learned here?

00:16:39.681 --> 00:16:43.481
To find out what is the will of God
and do it wholeheartedly.

00:16:46.321 --> 00:16:47.447
Maria...

00:16:48.957 --> 00:16:51.721
...it seems to be God's will
that you leave us.

00:16:51.993 --> 00:16:53.483
- Leave?
- Only for a while.

00:16:53.995 --> 00:16:56.327
No, Mother!
Please don't send me away!

00:16:56.565 --> 00:17:00.831
This is where I belong. It's my home,
my family. It's my life.

00:17:01.503 --> 00:17:04.529
- Are you truly ready for it?
- Yes, I am.

00:17:04.739 --> 00:17:09.642
If you go out into the world for a
time, knowing what we expect of you...

00:17:09.911 --> 00:17:12.641
...you will find out
if you can expect it of yourself.

00:17:12.847 --> 00:17:17.147
I know what you expect, Mother,
and I can do it! I promise I can!

00:17:20.689 --> 00:17:21.917
Yes, Mother.

00:17:24.025 --> 00:17:25.686
If it is God's will.

00:17:27.929 --> 00:17:33.060
There is a family near Salzburg that
needs a governess until September.

00:17:33.268 --> 00:17:35.498
- September?
- For seven children.

00:17:36.171 --> 00:17:37.160
Seven children?!

00:17:37.405 --> 00:17:38.667
Do you like children?

00:17:39.441 --> 00:17:41.272
Well, yes, but seven!

00:17:42.410 --> 00:17:45.573
I will tell Captain von Trapp
to expect you tomorrow.

00:17:46.114 --> 00:17:47.513
Captain?

00:17:48.216 --> 00:17:53.051
A retired officer of the Imperial
Navy. A fine man and a brave one.

00:17:53.288 --> 00:17:56.018
His wife died,
and he is alone with the children.

00:17:56.224 --> 00:18:00.524
I understand he has had a difficult
time keeping a governess there.

00:18:01.296 --> 00:18:03.594
Why difficult, Reverend Mother?

00:18:04.966 --> 00:18:07.901
The Lord will show you
in His own good time.

00:18:44.773 --> 00:18:47.241
When the Lord closes a door...

00:18:47.442 --> 00:18:49.967
...somewhere He opens a window.

00:18:52.314 --> 00:18:57.308
<i>What will this day be like?</i>

00:18:57.519 --> 00:18:59.749
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:06.261 --> 00:19:10.357
<i>What will my future be?</i>

00:19:11.199 --> 00:19:13.463
<i>I wonder</i>

00:19:15.036 --> 00:19:18.130
<i>It could be so exciting</i>

00:19:18.340 --> 00:19:21.434
<i>To be out in the world</i>
<i>To be free</i>

00:19:21.643 --> 00:19:24.703
<i>My heart should be wildly rejoicing</i>

00:19:25.880 --> 00:19:31.216
<i>Oh, what's the matter with me?</i>

00:19:31.553 --> 00:19:34.613
<i>I've always longed for adventure</i>

00:19:34.889 --> 00:19:38.450
<i>To do the things I've never dared</i>

00:19:38.693 --> 00:19:41.890
<i>Now here I'm facing adventure</i>

00:19:42.197 --> 00:19:48.295
<i>Then why am I so scared?</i>

00:19:51.740 --> 00:19:54.641
<i>A captain with seven children</i>

00:19:54.876 --> 00:19:57.709
<i>What's so fearsome about that?</i>

00:20:00.248 --> 00:20:02.876
<i>I must stop these doubts and worries</i>

00:20:03.151 --> 00:20:05.984
<i>If I don't I just know I'll turn back</i>

00:20:06.254 --> 00:20:09.417
<i>I must dream of the things</i>
<i>I am seeking</i>

00:20:10.492 --> 00:20:15.486
<i>I am seeking the courage I lack</i>

00:20:16.398 --> 00:20:20.232
<i>The courage to serve them</i>
<i>With reliance</i>

00:20:20.502 --> 00:20:23.403
<i>Face my mistakes without defiance</i>

00:20:23.671 --> 00:20:25.366
<i>Show them I'm worthy</i>

00:20:25.607 --> 00:20:28.269
<i>And while I show them</i>

00:20:28.543 --> 00:20:32.343
<i>I'll show me</i>

00:20:32.547 --> 00:20:37.951
<i>So let them bring on</i>
<i>All their problems</i>

00:20:38.186 --> 00:20:41.451
<i>I'll do better than my best</i>

00:20:41.723 --> 00:20:44.783
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>They'll put me to the test</i>

00:20:45.026 --> 00:20:48.462
<i>But I'll make them see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:20:48.696 --> 00:20:51.961
<i>Somehow I will impress them</i>

00:20:52.233 --> 00:20:55.464
<i>I will be firm but kind</i>

00:20:55.737 --> 00:20:59.036
<i>And all those children</i>
<i>Heaven bless them</i>

00:20:59.274 --> 00:21:02.573
<i>They will look up to me</i>
<i>And mind me</i>

00:21:02.811 --> 00:21:05.939
<i>With each step I am more certain</i>

00:21:06.214 --> 00:21:09.479
<i>Everything will turn out fine</i>

00:21:09.717 --> 00:21:12.811
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>The world can all be mine</i>

00:21:13.054 --> 00:21:18.492
<i>They'll have to agree</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:20.061 --> 00:21:22.791
<i>I have confidence in sunshine</i>

00:21:23.064 --> 00:21:26.158
<i>I have confidence in rain</i>

00:21:26.401 --> 00:21:29.268
<i>I have confidence</i>
<i>That spring will come again</i>

00:21:29.571 --> 00:21:32.597
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence in me</i>

00:21:32.907 --> 00:21:35.967
<i>Strength doesn't lie in numbers</i>

00:21:36.244 --> 00:21:39.270
<i>Strength doesn't lie in wealth</i>

00:21:39.514 --> 00:21:42.847
<i>Strength lies in nights</i>
<i>Of peaceful slumbers</i>

00:21:43.117 --> 00:21:45.984
<i>When you wake up, wake up</i>
<i>It's healthy</i>

00:21:46.287 --> 00:21:49.279
<i>All I trust I leave my heart to</i>

00:21:49.524 --> 00:21:52.425
<i>All I trust becomes my own</i>

00:21:52.627 --> 00:21:57.428
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:12.046 --> 00:22:13.673
Oh, help.

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:32.527
<i>I have confidence in confidence alone</i>

00:22:33.334 --> 00:22:38.135
<i>Besides which you see</i>
<i>I have confidence...</i>

00:22:38.406 --> 00:22:45.209
<i>...in me</i>

00:22:51.753 --> 00:22:54.153
Hello. Here I am.

00:22:56.991 --> 00:22:58.822
I'm from the convent.
I'm the new governess, captain.

00:23:00.495 --> 00:23:03.726
And I'm the old butler, fräulein.

00:23:05.700 --> 00:23:07.497
Well, how do you do?

00:23:18.012 --> 00:23:22.073
You'll wait here, please.

00:24:48.436 --> 00:24:52.532
In future, remember certain rooms
in this house are not to be disturbed.

00:24:53.708 --> 00:24:55.175
Yes, captain, sir.

00:25:03.117 --> 00:25:08.350
- Why do you stare at me that way?
- You don't look like a sea captain.

00:25:09.557 --> 00:25:12.617
I'm afraid you don't look
very much like a governess.

00:25:13.327 --> 00:25:14.385
- Turn around.
- What?

00:25:14.729 --> 00:25:15.991
Turn.

00:25:19.167 --> 00:25:20.327
Hat off.

00:25:23.538 --> 00:25:26.166
Put on another dress
before meeting the children.

00:25:26.474 --> 00:25:28.032
But I don't have another.

00:25:28.309 --> 00:25:31.176
When we enter the abbey,
our worldly clothes go to the poor.

00:25:31.412 --> 00:25:32.674
What about this one?

00:25:32.880 --> 00:25:34.211
The poor didn't want it.

00:25:36.050 --> 00:25:39.542
There wasn't time to make a new dress.
I can make clothes.

00:25:40.822 --> 00:25:43.086
I'll see that you get some material.

00:25:43.825 --> 00:25:45.349
Today, if possible.

00:25:46.327 --> 00:25:48.090
- Now, fräulein...
- Maria.

00:25:48.329 --> 00:25:51.059
I don't know how much
the abbess told you.

00:25:51.332 --> 00:25:53.892
You are the twelfth governess...

00:25:54.102 --> 00:25:56.570
...to look after my children
since their mother died.

00:25:56.771 --> 00:25:59.001
I trust you will be an improvement
on the last one.

00:25:59.240 --> 00:26:01.071
She stayed only two hours.

00:26:02.777 --> 00:26:05.371
What's wrong with the children, sir?

00:26:06.848 --> 00:26:11.251
Nothing is wrong with the children,
only the governesses.

00:26:11.519 --> 00:26:16.456
They could not maintain discipline,
without which the house cannot be run.

00:26:17.391 --> 00:26:19.188
Drill them in their studies.

00:26:19.427 --> 00:26:22.919
I will not permit them to dream
away their summer holidays.

00:26:23.197 --> 00:26:25.893
Each afternoon,
they march, breathing deeply.

00:26:26.100 --> 00:26:27.761
Bedtime is to be strictly observed.

00:26:27.969 --> 00:26:28.936
When do they play?

00:26:29.137 --> 00:26:33.198
You will see to it that they conduct
themselves with the utmost decorum.

00:26:33.441 --> 00:26:36.376
- I am placing you in command.
- Yes, sir.

00:27:57.024 --> 00:27:58.184
Now...

00:27:58.793 --> 00:28:01.728
...this is your new governess,
Fräulein Maria.

00:28:03.397 --> 00:28:05.388
Give your name at your signal.

00:28:05.700 --> 00:28:09.898
Fräulein, listen carefully. Learn
their signals so you can call them.

00:28:11.205 --> 00:28:12.570
Liesl.

00:28:12.840 --> 00:28:14.569
Friedrich.

00:28:14.842 --> 00:28:16.366
Louisa.

00:28:16.644 --> 00:28:17.906
Kurt.

00:28:18.145 --> 00:28:19.203
Brigitta.

00:28:19.480 --> 00:28:20.708
Marta.

00:28:27.088 --> 00:28:28.419
Gretl.

00:28:33.060 --> 00:28:36.496
Now, let's see how well you listened.

00:28:36.731 --> 00:28:39.097
I won't need to whistle for them,
Reverend Captain.

00:28:39.367 --> 00:28:42.825
I mean, I'll use their names.
Such lovely names.

00:28:43.037 --> 00:28:46.200
Fräulein, this is a large house.
The grounds are extensive.

00:28:46.440 --> 00:28:49.204
And I will not have anyone shouting.

00:28:49.443 --> 00:28:51.172
You will take this, please.
Learn to use it.

00:28:51.379 --> 00:28:53.040
The children will help you.

00:28:55.082 --> 00:28:59.075
Now, when I want you,
this is what you will hear.

00:28:59.954 --> 00:29:01.751
Oh, no, sir. I'm sorry, sir!

00:29:02.623 --> 00:29:04.181
I could never answer to a whistle.

00:29:04.392 --> 00:29:07.020
Whistles are for animals,
not for children.

00:29:07.295 --> 00:29:09.354
And definitely not for me.

00:29:09.597 --> 00:29:12.225
It would be too humiliating.

00:29:13.034 --> 00:29:18.233
Fräulein, were you this much trouble
at the abbey?

00:29:18.539 --> 00:29:19.631
Oh, much more, sir.

00:29:30.751 --> 00:29:32.309
I don't know your signal.

00:29:33.788 --> 00:29:36.416
You may call me "captain."

00:29:49.337 --> 00:29:50.804
At ease.

00:29:53.607 --> 00:29:55.165
Now that there's just us...

00:29:55.443 --> 00:29:59.607
...would you please tell me all your
names again and how old you are.

00:30:00.081 --> 00:30:04.074
I'm Liesl. I'm 16 years old,
and I don't need a governess.

00:30:04.852 --> 00:30:07.912
I'm glad you told me, Liesl.
We'll just be good friends.

00:30:10.091 --> 00:30:13.857
I'm Friedrich. I'm 14.
I'm impossible.

00:30:14.161 --> 00:30:15.822
Really? Who told you that, Friedrich?

00:30:16.097 --> 00:30:19.589
Fräulein Josephine.
Four governesses ago.

00:30:20.034 --> 00:30:21.501
I'm Brigitta.

00:30:23.337 --> 00:30:27.330
You didn't tell me how old you are,
Louisa.

00:30:28.009 --> 00:30:30.273
I'm Brigitta. She's Louisa.

00:30:30.511 --> 00:30:33.275
She's 13 years old, and you're smart.

00:30:33.514 --> 00:30:37.280
I'm 10, and I think your dress
is the ugliest one I ever saw.

00:30:37.618 --> 00:30:40.246
- Brigitta, you shouldn't say that.
- Why not?

00:30:40.454 --> 00:30:42.718
- Don't you think it's ugly?
- Of course.

00:30:42.990 --> 00:30:45.686
But Fräulein Helga's was ugliest.

00:30:45.960 --> 00:30:48.554
I'm Kurt. I'm 11.
I'm incorrigible.

00:30:48.829 --> 00:30:51.957
- Congratulations.
- What's "incorrigible"?

00:30:52.199 --> 00:30:56.067
I think it means you want
to be treated like a boy.

00:30:58.239 --> 00:31:01.538
I'm Marta, and I'm going to be
seven on Tuesday.

00:31:01.809 --> 00:31:03.174
I'd like a pink parasol.

00:31:04.378 --> 00:31:05.902
Pink's my favorite color too.

00:31:08.315 --> 00:31:09.475
Yes, you're Gretl.

00:31:10.384 --> 00:31:12.079
And you're five years old?

00:31:12.520 --> 00:31:14.511
My, you're practically a lady.

00:31:17.024 --> 00:31:20.050
I have to tell you a secret.
I've never been a governess.

00:31:21.495 --> 00:31:24.259
You don't know anything
about being a governess?

00:31:24.532 --> 00:31:25.897
Nothing. I'll need lots of advice.

00:31:26.867 --> 00:31:31.395
The best way to start is to tell
Father to mind his own business.

00:31:31.605 --> 00:31:33.402
Never come to dinner on time.

00:31:33.607 --> 00:31:35.905
Never eat your soup quietly.

00:31:36.577 --> 00:31:38.670
During dessert, always blow your nose.

00:31:38.913 --> 00:31:41.711
Don't you believe a word they say,
Fräulein Maria.

00:31:41.916 --> 00:31:45.283
- Oh, why not?
- Because I like you.

00:31:46.087 --> 00:31:48.078
Children, outside for your walk.

00:31:48.289 --> 00:31:50.189
Father's orders. Hurry up.

00:31:50.391 --> 00:31:51.688
Quick, quick, quick.

00:31:51.926 --> 00:31:55.123
Fräulein Maria, I'm Frau Schmidt,
the housekeeper.

00:31:55.362 --> 00:31:56.420
How do you do.

00:31:56.630 --> 00:31:59.531
I'll show you to your room.
Follow me.

00:32:10.611 --> 00:32:12.374
Poor little dears.

00:32:25.092 --> 00:32:29.461
You're very lucky. With
Fräulein Helga it was a snake.

00:32:43.310 --> 00:32:44.641
Good evening.

00:32:46.080 --> 00:32:49.641
- Good evening, children.
- Good evening, Fräulein Maria.

00:32:56.857 --> 00:32:58.484
Enchanting little ritual.

00:32:58.692 --> 00:33:01.422
Something you learned at the abbey?

00:33:02.630 --> 00:33:04.962
No.

00:33:06.600 --> 00:33:07.862
Rheumatism.

00:33:17.678 --> 00:33:20.841
Excuse me, captain. Haven't we
forgotten to thank the Lord?

00:33:29.056 --> 00:33:32.025
For what we receive,
may the Lord make us truly thankful.

00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:34.494
- Amen.
- Amen.

00:33:39.033 --> 00:33:40.967
I'd like to thank you all...

00:33:41.168 --> 00:33:44.160
...for the precious gift
you left in my pocket today.

00:33:47.675 --> 00:33:49.472
What gift?

00:33:52.580 --> 00:33:54.741
It's a secret between
the children and me.

00:33:55.015 --> 00:33:58.644
Then I suggest you keep it,
and let us eat.

00:33:59.019 --> 00:34:00.987
Knowing how nervous
I must have been...

00:34:01.222 --> 00:34:03.656
...a stranger in a new household...

00:34:03.857 --> 00:34:06.917
...knowing how important it was
for me to feel accepted...

00:34:07.194 --> 00:34:11.392
...it was so kind and thoughtful of
you to make my first moments here...

00:34:11.665 --> 00:34:13.860
...so warm and happy...

00:34:14.068 --> 00:34:15.831
...and pleasant.

00:34:25.079 --> 00:34:27.104
- What is the matter, Marta?
- Nothing.

00:34:39.526 --> 00:34:40.550
Fräulein...

00:34:40.794 --> 00:34:44.628
...is it to be at every meal
or merely at dinnertime...

00:34:44.865 --> 00:34:49.427
...that you intend leading us through
this rare and wonderful new world...

00:34:49.637 --> 00:34:51.298
...of indigestion?

00:34:52.873 --> 00:34:55.740
They're all right, captain.
They're just happy.

00:35:14.495 --> 00:35:17.157
- Rolfe, good evening.
- Good evening, Franz.

00:35:17.431 --> 00:35:20.161
- I trust everything is under control?
- Yes, yes.

00:35:21.802 --> 00:35:24.236
- Are there any developments?
- Perhaps.

00:35:24.438 --> 00:35:26.599
- Is the captain home?
- He's at dinner.

00:35:26.840 --> 00:35:29.172
- With the family?
- Yes.

00:35:29.443 --> 00:35:31.240
Give him this telegram at once.

00:35:31.979 --> 00:35:33.071
Certainly.

00:35:44.758 --> 00:35:46.453
A telegram for you, sir.

00:35:49.296 --> 00:35:51.127
Franz? Who delivered it?

00:35:51.432 --> 00:35:53.457
That young lad Rolfe, of course.

00:35:55.803 --> 00:35:57.532
Father, may I be excused?

00:35:58.505 --> 00:36:02.965
Children, in the morning I shall
be going to Vienna.

00:36:03.277 --> 00:36:05.711
Not again, Father!

00:36:09.616 --> 00:36:11.675
How long will you be gone this time?

00:36:12.319 --> 00:36:13.786
I'm not sure, Gretl.

00:36:13.987 --> 00:36:17.548
- To visit Baroness Schraeder again?
- Mind your own business!

00:36:18.525 --> 00:36:20.459
As a matter of fact, yes, Louisa.

00:36:22.229 --> 00:36:26.063
- Why can't we ever see the baroness?
- Why would she want to see you?

00:36:26.367 --> 00:36:31.236
You are going to see the baroness.
I'm bringing her back with me to visit.

00:36:32.740 --> 00:36:34.537
And Uncle Max.

00:36:34.808 --> 00:36:37.208
Uncle Max!

00:36:53.260 --> 00:36:54.591
Rolfe!

00:36:57.664 --> 00:36:58.722
Oh, Rolfe!

00:37:01.268 --> 00:37:04.203
- No, Liesl. We mustn't!
- Why not, silly?

00:37:04.438 --> 00:37:07.100
- I don't know...
- Isn't this why you're waiting?

00:37:07.341 --> 00:37:09.206
Yes, of course.

00:37:09.410 --> 00:37:12.208
- I've missed you, Liesl.
- You have? How much?

00:37:12.446 --> 00:37:16.280
I even thought of sending a telegram,
so I'd be able to deliver it here.

00:37:16.550 --> 00:37:20.452
Oh, that's a lovely thought!
Why don't you, right now?

00:37:20.721 --> 00:37:24.885
- But I'm here!
- Please, Rolfe. Send me a telegram.

00:37:25.092 --> 00:37:28.550
I'll start it for you.
"Dear Liesl..."

00:37:29.229 --> 00:37:32.858
"Dear Liesl: I'd like to be able
to tell you...

00:37:33.100 --> 00:37:35.295
...how I feel about you. Stop.

00:37:35.536 --> 00:37:40.064
Unfortunately, this wire
is already too expensive.

00:37:40.274 --> 00:37:41.707
Sincerely, Rolfe."

00:37:41.909 --> 00:37:44.673
- "Sincerely"?
- Cordially.

00:37:44.878 --> 00:37:47.540
- "Cordially"?
- Affectionately?

00:37:49.917 --> 00:37:51.942
Will there be any reply?

00:37:53.220 --> 00:37:55.381
"Dear Rolfe: Stop.

00:37:56.390 --> 00:37:59.484
Don't stop! Your Liesl."

00:38:01.228 --> 00:38:05.062
If only we didn't have to wait
for someone to send Father a telegram.

00:38:05.332 --> 00:38:07.732
How do I know when I'll see you again?

00:38:08.635 --> 00:38:09.829
Well, let's see...

00:38:12.840 --> 00:38:14.808
I could come here by mistake.

00:38:15.809 --> 00:38:20.439
With a telegram for Colonel Schneider!
He's here from Berlin staying with...

00:38:21.348 --> 00:38:24.647
No one knows he's here.
Don't tell your father.

00:38:24.918 --> 00:38:28.081
- Why not?
- Your father's so Austrian.

00:38:28.288 --> 00:38:29.585
We're all Austrian.

00:38:29.790 --> 00:38:34.193
Some think we ought to be German, and
they're very mad at those who don't.

00:38:34.428 --> 00:38:36.191
They're getting ready to...

00:38:37.865 --> 00:38:40.299
Let's hope your father
doesn't get into trouble.

00:38:40.601 --> 00:38:45.504
Don't worry. He's a big naval hero.
He was even decorated by the emperor.

00:38:45.706 --> 00:38:48.971
I don't worry about him.
I worry about his daughter.

00:38:49.510 --> 00:38:50.977
Me? Why?

00:38:51.278 --> 00:38:52.836
- Well, you're so...
- What?

00:38:53.280 --> 00:38:54.770
You're such a baby!

00:38:55.215 --> 00:38:58.116
I'm 16.
What's such a baby about that?

00:39:00.354 --> 00:39:03.881
<i>You wait, little girl</i>
<i>On an empty stage</i>

00:39:04.124 --> 00:39:07.491
<i>For fate to turn the light on</i>

00:39:08.128 --> 00:39:11.359
<i>Your life, little girl</i>
<i>Is an empty page</i>

00:39:11.632 --> 00:39:15.693
<i>That men will want to write on</i>

00:39:16.403 --> 00:39:21.898
<i>To write on</i>

00:39:22.843 --> 00:39:26.779
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:26.980 --> 00:39:30.814
<i>Baby, it's time to think</i>

00:39:31.018 --> 00:39:34.647
<i>Better beware</i>
<i>Be canny and careful</i>

00:39:34.888 --> 00:39:38.517
<i>Baby, you're on the brink</i>

00:39:38.859 --> 00:39:42.693
<i>You are 16 going on 17</i>

00:39:42.896 --> 00:39:46.559
<i>Fellows will fall in line</i>

00:39:46.867 --> 00:39:50.200
<i>Eager young lads</i>
<i>And roués and cads</i>

00:39:50.404 --> 00:39:54.340
<i>Will offer you food and wine</i>

00:39:54.608 --> 00:39:58.374
<i>Totally unprepared are you</i>

00:39:58.779 --> 00:40:02.340
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:40:02.916 --> 00:40:07.080
<i>Timid and shy and scared are you</i>

00:40:07.387 --> 00:40:10.879
<i>Of things beyond your ken</i>

00:40:11.091 --> 00:40:14.959
<i>You need someone older and wiser</i>

00:40:15.195 --> 00:40:19.063
<i>Telling you what to do</i>

00:40:19.299 --> 00:40:22.735
<i>I am 17 going on 18</i>

00:40:22.970 --> 00:40:28.931
<i>I'll take care of you</i>

00:41:01.475 --> 00:41:04.808
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:05.012 --> 00:41:08.413
<i>I know that I'm naive</i>

00:41:08.682 --> 00:41:11.913
<i>Fellows I meet</i>
<i>May tell me I'm sweet</i>

00:41:12.152 --> 00:41:15.849
<i>And willingly I believe</i>

00:41:16.323 --> 00:41:19.486
<i>I am 16 going on 17</i>

00:41:19.693 --> 00:41:23.459
<i>Innocent as a rose</i>

00:41:23.664 --> 00:41:27.122
<i>Bachelor dandies</i>
<i>Drinkers of brandies</i>

00:41:27.434 --> 00:41:30.767
<i>What do I know of those?</i>

00:41:30.971 --> 00:41:34.498
<i>Totally unprepared am I</i>

00:41:34.775 --> 00:41:38.267
<i>To face a world of men</i>

00:41:38.679 --> 00:41:42.012
<i>Timid and shy and scared am I</i>

00:41:42.282 --> 00:41:45.945
<i>Of things beyond my ken</i>

00:41:46.386 --> 00:41:49.981
<i>I need someone older and wiser</i>

00:41:50.223 --> 00:41:53.522
<i>Telling me what to do</i>

00:41:53.860 --> 00:41:57.557
<i>You are 17 going on 18</i>

00:41:57.798 --> 00:42:03.464
<i>I'll depend on you</i>

00:43:56.516 --> 00:43:57.949
Come in.

00:43:58.985 --> 00:44:00.612
Frau Schmidt.

00:44:02.956 --> 00:44:04.685
For your new dresses.

00:44:04.991 --> 00:44:08.984
- The captain had these sent from town.
- Oh, how lovely!

00:44:09.262 --> 00:44:12.698
These will make the prettiest
clothes I've ever had.

00:44:12.966 --> 00:44:16.458
Do you think he would
get me more material if I asked?

00:44:16.703 --> 00:44:20.332
- How many dresses do you need?
- Not for me, for the children.

00:44:20.607 --> 00:44:22.666
I want to make them some play clothes.

00:44:22.943 --> 00:44:26.470
The von Trapp children don't play.
They march.

00:44:26.980 --> 00:44:29.380
Surely you don't approve of that.

00:44:30.383 --> 00:44:32.783
Ever since the captain
lost his poor wife...

00:44:33.019 --> 00:44:35.715
...he runs this house as if on
one of his ships.

00:44:36.556 --> 00:44:37.955
Whistles, orders.

00:44:38.225 --> 00:44:40.056
No more music, no more laughing.

00:44:40.327 --> 00:44:43.854
Nothing that reminds him of her.
Even the children.

00:44:44.364 --> 00:44:45.456
But that's so wrong.

00:44:46.299 --> 00:44:47.823
Oh, well.

00:44:48.034 --> 00:44:51.697
How do you like your room?
There'll be new drapes at the windows.

00:44:51.972 --> 00:44:53.234
Bu these are fine.

00:44:53.473 --> 00:44:55.134
New ones have been ordered.

00:44:55.342 --> 00:44:58.641
- But I really don't need them.
- Good night, now.

00:44:58.879 --> 00:45:02.906
Frau Schmidt, if I asked
the captain about the material...?

00:45:03.183 --> 00:45:07.643
- He's leaving in the morning.
- Of course. How long will he be gone?

00:45:08.221 --> 00:45:12.817
It depends. The last time he visited
the baroness, he stayed for a month.

00:45:13.994 --> 00:45:18.556
I shouldn't be saying this to you.
I don't know you that well.

00:45:18.832 --> 00:45:21.733
But if you ask me,
the captain's thinking seriously...

00:45:21.935 --> 00:45:24.233
...of marrying her before
summer's over.

00:45:24.437 --> 00:45:27.668
Wonderful! The children will
have a mother again.

00:45:29.109 --> 00:45:30.406
Yes.

00:45:30.677 --> 00:45:32.406
Well, good night.

00:45:32.612 --> 00:45:34.045
Good night.

00:45:52.465 --> 00:45:55.298
Dear Father, now I know
why You sent me here.

00:45:55.535 --> 00:45:58.402
To help these children
prepare for a new mother.

00:45:58.638 --> 00:46:01.937
And I pray this will become
a happy family in Thy sight.

00:46:02.142 --> 00:46:05.270
God bless the captain.
God bless Liesl and Friedrich.

00:46:05.478 --> 00:46:09.642
God bless Louisa, Brigitta,
Marta and little Gretl.

00:46:09.950 --> 00:46:12.783
And I forgot the other boy.
What's his name?

00:46:14.554 --> 00:46:16.385
Well, God bless what's-his-name.

00:46:16.589 --> 00:46:20.582
God bless the Reverend Mother
and Sister Margaretta...

00:46:20.794 --> 00:46:22.591
...and everybody at the abbey.

00:46:22.796 --> 00:46:25.321
And now, dear God, about Liesl.

00:46:25.832 --> 00:46:27.732
Help her know that I'm her friend...

00:46:27.934 --> 00:46:30.494
...and help her tell me
what she's been up to.

00:46:31.237 --> 00:46:32.397
Are you going to tell on me?

00:46:32.639 --> 00:46:36.075
Help me to be understanding
so I may guide her footsteps.

00:46:36.343 --> 00:46:38.971
In the name of the Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost.

00:46:39.179 --> 00:46:42.171
I was out walking
and somebody locked the doors early.

00:46:42.482 --> 00:46:46.111
I didn't want to wake everybody,
so when I saw your window open...

00:46:47.754 --> 00:46:50.780
You're not going to tell Father,
are you?

00:46:56.863 --> 00:46:58.160
How did you climb up?

00:46:58.665 --> 00:47:01.793
It's how we always got in
to play tricks on the governess.

00:47:02.002 --> 00:47:04.994
Louisa can make it with
a whole jar of spiders in her hand.

00:47:06.006 --> 00:47:07.667
Spiders?

00:47:11.378 --> 00:47:14.006
Were you out walking all by yourself?

00:47:21.488 --> 00:47:25.185
If we wash that dress tonight,
nobody would notice it tomorrow.

00:47:25.859 --> 00:47:27.622
You could put this on.

00:47:29.362 --> 00:47:32.058
Take your dress and put it
to soak in the bathtub.

00:47:32.298 --> 00:47:35.825
Come back here and sit on the bed,
and we'll have a talk.

00:47:37.137 --> 00:47:40.163
I told you today
I didn't need a governess.

00:47:40.373 --> 00:47:42.466
Well, maybe I do.

00:48:12.939 --> 00:48:15.499
Gretl, are you scared?

00:48:19.012 --> 00:48:21.276
You're not frightened
of a storm, are you?

00:48:21.514 --> 00:48:23.778
You just stay right here with me.

00:48:24.951 --> 00:48:29.183
- Where are the others?
- They're asleep. They're not scared.

00:48:33.593 --> 00:48:35.424
Oh, no? Look.

00:48:36.963 --> 00:48:38.931
All right, up here on the bed.

00:48:39.232 --> 00:48:41.928
- Really?
- Well, just this once. Come on.

00:48:43.036 --> 00:48:47.370
- Now we'll wait for the boys.
- You won't see them. Boys are brave.

00:48:53.446 --> 00:48:55.243
You weren't scared, were you?

00:48:55.782 --> 00:48:58.979
Oh, no. We just wanted
to be sure that you weren't.

00:49:00.086 --> 00:49:03.112
- That's very thoughtful of you.
- It wasn't my idea.

00:49:03.423 --> 00:49:05.254
It was Kurt's!

00:49:05.492 --> 00:49:08.086
Kurt! That's the one I left out!
God bless Kurt.

00:49:10.897 --> 00:49:12.660
Why does it do that?

00:49:12.899 --> 00:49:16.733
The lightning talks to the thunder,
and the thunder answers.

00:49:16.970 --> 00:49:19.461
- But lightning must be nasty.
- Not really.

00:49:19.739 --> 00:49:22.003
Why does the thunder get so angry?

00:49:22.275 --> 00:49:24.402
It makes me want to cry.

00:49:26.279 --> 00:49:30.477
Whenever I'm feeling unhappy,
I just try to think of nice things.

00:49:30.683 --> 00:49:32.514
What kind of things?

00:49:33.286 --> 00:49:35.254
Well, let me see. Nice things...

00:49:35.488 --> 00:49:36.580
Daffodils.

00:49:37.857 --> 00:49:39.256
Green meadows.

00:49:39.659 --> 00:49:41.923
Skies full of stars.

00:49:42.128 --> 00:49:45.325
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>and whiskers on kittens</i>

00:49:45.532 --> 00:49:48.660
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:49:48.868 --> 00:49:52.031
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:49:52.305 --> 00:49:56.298
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:49:58.878 --> 00:50:01.676
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:50:01.948 --> 00:50:05.145
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:50:05.385 --> 00:50:08.320
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:50:08.555 --> 00:50:12.389
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:13.660 --> 00:50:16.390
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:50:16.663 --> 00:50:19.860
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:50:20.133 --> 00:50:23.193
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:50:23.469 --> 00:50:26.836
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:50:27.040 --> 00:50:28.735
<i>When the dog bites</i>

00:50:28.975 --> 00:50:30.636
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:50:30.877 --> 00:50:33.141
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:50:33.379 --> 00:50:36.746
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:50:37.016 --> 00:50:43.854
<i>And then I don't feel so bad</i>

00:50:44.591 --> 00:50:46.252
- Does it work?
- Of course.

00:50:46.559 --> 00:50:48.493
- What do you like?
- Pussy willow!

00:50:49.195 --> 00:50:51.425
- Christmas!
- Bunny rabbits!

00:50:51.664 --> 00:50:53.325
Snakes!

00:50:53.600 --> 00:50:55.727
- Chocolate icing!
- No school!

00:50:56.035 --> 00:50:57.161
Pillow fights!

00:50:57.437 --> 00:50:59.428
- Telegrams!
- Birthday presents!

00:50:59.839 --> 00:51:02.205
- Any presents!
- Ladybugs!

00:51:03.710 --> 00:51:05.041
A good sneeze!

00:51:05.345 --> 00:51:07.074
Gesundheit!

00:51:07.380 --> 00:51:08.608
See what fun it is?

00:51:08.848 --> 00:51:11.783
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

00:51:12.051 --> 00:51:14.918
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

00:51:15.188 --> 00:51:18.180
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

00:51:18.424 --> 00:51:21.257
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:24.697 --> 00:51:27.530
<i>Cream-colored ponies</i>
<i>And crisp apple strudels</i>

00:51:27.767 --> 00:51:30.634
<i>Doorbells and sleigh bells</i>
<i>And schnitzel with noodles</i>

00:51:30.870 --> 00:51:33.805
<i>Wild geese that fly</i>
<i>With the moon on their wings</i>

00:51:34.073 --> 00:51:37.565
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:38.544 --> 00:51:40.034
Together.

00:51:40.313 --> 00:51:43.077
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:51:43.316 --> 00:51:46.217
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

00:51:46.452 --> 00:51:49.444
<i>Silver white winters</i>
<i>That melt into springs</i>

00:51:49.722 --> 00:51:52.987
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

00:51:53.293 --> 00:51:55.420
<i>When the dog bi...</i>

00:51:55.628 --> 00:51:57.596
Dog bites.

00:52:04.237 --> 00:52:05.465
Hello.

00:52:05.672 --> 00:52:09.836
Fräulein, did I not tell you that
bedtime is to be strictly observed?

00:52:10.143 --> 00:52:12.839
The children were upset
by the storm, so l...

00:52:14.247 --> 00:52:15.236
You did, sir.

00:52:15.448 --> 00:52:19.646
Do you, or do you not, have difficulty
remembering such simple instructions?

00:52:20.953 --> 00:52:22.580
Only during thunderstorms.

00:52:25.091 --> 00:52:26.581
Liesl?

00:52:26.826 --> 00:52:29.021
I don't recall seeing you
after dinner.

00:52:29.629 --> 00:52:31.358
Really? As a matter of fact...

00:52:31.631 --> 00:52:32.859
Yes?

00:52:33.666 --> 00:52:34.826
Well, I was...

00:52:35.101 --> 00:52:37.160
What she would like to say...

00:52:37.370 --> 00:52:40.271
...is that she and I have
been getting acquainted tonight.

00:52:40.473 --> 00:52:45.342
It's too late to go into that. You
heard your father. Go back to bed.

00:52:49.982 --> 00:52:51.381
Fräulein...

00:52:51.684 --> 00:52:55.711
...you have managed to remember
I'm leaving in the morning?

00:52:56.823 --> 00:53:01.351
Is it also possible you remember the
first rule in this house is discipline?

00:53:03.029 --> 00:53:05.520
Then I trust that before I return...

00:53:06.032 --> 00:53:07.795
...you'll have acquired some?

00:53:09.168 --> 00:53:10.533
Captain?

00:53:11.504 --> 00:53:15.406
Could I talk to you about clothes
for the children for when they play?

00:53:15.675 --> 00:53:18.371
- If I could have some material.
- You are many things.

00:53:18.644 --> 00:53:20.805
Not the least of which is repetitious.

00:53:21.013 --> 00:53:23.174
- But they're children!
- Yes.

00:53:23.416 --> 00:53:25.179
And I'm their father.

00:53:25.752 --> 00:53:26.980
Good night.

00:53:51.244 --> 00:53:57.080
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

00:54:08.594 --> 00:54:12.121
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

00:54:12.365 --> 00:54:14.856
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

00:54:15.101 --> 00:54:18.400
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

00:54:18.604 --> 00:54:20.731
<i>And then I don't feel...</i>

00:54:20.973 --> 00:54:27.902
<i>...so bad</i>

00:54:51.904 --> 00:54:54.600
Children, over here. See!

00:54:58.244 --> 00:54:59.609
Come on.

00:56:22.662 --> 00:56:23.890
Fräulein Maria?

00:56:24.163 --> 00:56:26.063
Can we do this every day?

00:56:26.365 --> 00:56:29.562
- Don't you think you'd get tired of it?
- I suppose so.

00:56:29.902 --> 00:56:31.164
Every other day?

00:56:31.370 --> 00:56:36.000
I haven't had so much fun since we put
glue on Fräulein Josephine's toothbrush.

00:56:36.208 --> 00:56:40.110
I can't understand how children
as nice as you can play such tricks.

00:56:40.379 --> 00:56:42.210
- It's easy.
- But why do it?

00:56:42.415 --> 00:56:44.849
How else can we get
Father's attention?

00:56:45.618 --> 00:56:47.210
Oh, I see.

00:56:48.554 --> 00:56:50.749
We'll have to think about that one.

00:56:52.925 --> 00:56:54.552
All right, over here.

00:56:54.760 --> 00:56:56.193
What are we going to do?

00:56:56.429 --> 00:56:58.397
Think of a song for the baroness.

00:56:58.631 --> 00:57:00.599
Father doesn't like us to sing.

00:57:00.866 --> 00:57:04.427
Perhaps we can change his mind.
Now, what songs do you know?

00:57:04.704 --> 00:57:06.865
We don't know any songs.

00:57:07.106 --> 00:57:09.768
- Not any?
- We don't even know how to sing.

00:57:11.444 --> 00:57:13.605
Let's not lose time. You must learn.

00:57:13.879 --> 00:57:15.608
But how?

00:57:19.919 --> 00:57:23.878
<i>Let's start at the very beginning</i>

00:57:24.090 --> 00:57:27.457
<i>A very good place to start</i>

00:57:27.660 --> 00:57:29.594
<i>When you read you begin with</i>

00:57:29.829 --> 00:57:31.057
<i>A, B, C</i>

00:57:31.263 --> 00:57:35.597
<i>When you sing, you begin with</i>
<i>Do-Re-Mi</i>

00:57:35.835 --> 00:57:37.462
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:37.737 --> 00:57:39.068
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:39.305 --> 00:57:43.139
<i>The first three notes</i>
<i>Just happen to be</i>

00:57:43.409 --> 00:57:45.172
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:45.411 --> 00:57:46.673
<i>Do-re-mi</i>

00:57:46.912 --> 00:57:50.848
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti</i>

00:57:51.517 --> 00:57:53.951
Let's see if I can make it easier.

00:57:57.356 --> 00:58:01.019
<i>"Doe," a deer</i>
<i>A female deer</i>

00:58:01.260 --> 00:58:04.821
<i>"Ray," a drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:05.097 --> 00:58:08.863
<i>"Me," a name I call myself</i>

00:58:09.135 --> 00:58:12.832
<i>"Far," a long long way to run</i>

00:58:13.105 --> 00:58:16.871
<i>"Sew," a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:17.176 --> 00:58:21.010
<i>"La," a note to follow sew</i>

00:58:21.280 --> 00:58:24.215
<i>"Tea," a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:24.684 --> 00:58:28.780
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:58:29.288 --> 00:58:32.849
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:58:33.125 --> 00:58:36.322
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

00:58:36.562 --> 00:58:39.861
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

00:58:40.132 --> 00:58:43.226
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

00:58:43.736 --> 00:58:47.194
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:58:47.406 --> 00:58:50.739
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

00:58:51.177 --> 00:58:54.044
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

00:58:54.313 --> 00:58:56.577
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

00:58:56.816 --> 00:59:00.252
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

00:59:00.519 --> 00:59:03.579
<i>Ray, a drop of golden sun</i>

00:59:04.056 --> 00:59:07.253
<i>Me, a name I call myself</i>

00:59:07.526 --> 00:59:10.586
<i>Far, a long long way to run</i>

00:59:10.863 --> 00:59:14.094
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

00:59:14.400 --> 00:59:17.767
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

00:59:18.037 --> 00:59:20.665
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

00:59:20.873 --> 00:59:24.934
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

00:59:25.344 --> 00:59:28.438
<i>Do-re-mi-fa-so-la-ti-do, so-do</i>

00:59:28.881 --> 00:59:33.443
Do-re-mi-fa-so and so on are only
the tools we use to build a song.

00:59:33.719 --> 00:59:36.950
Once you have them in your head
you can sing different tunes...

00:59:37.223 --> 00:59:39.350
...by mixing them up. Like this:

00:59:40.593 --> 00:59:46.088
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:46.298 --> 00:59:47.390
Can you do that?

00:59:47.600 --> 00:59:53.095
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

00:59:53.305 --> 00:59:58.971
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

00:59:59.278 --> 01:00:04.580
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:04.784 --> 01:00:06.547
Now, put it all together.

01:00:06.752 --> 01:00:13.385
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:00:13.626 --> 01:00:19.587
<i>So-do-la-ti-do-re-do</i>

01:00:20.166 --> 01:00:22.760
- Good.
- But it doesn't mean anything.

01:00:23.002 --> 01:00:25.971
So we put in words.
One word for every note.

01:00:26.238 --> 01:00:27.500
Like this:

01:00:27.740 --> 01:00:34.304
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:34.580 --> 01:00:40.177
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:40.452 --> 01:00:41.419
Together!

01:00:41.620 --> 01:00:48.321
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:00:48.527 --> 01:00:55.194
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:00:55.601 --> 01:00:58.968
<i>- Doe</i>
<i>- A deer, a female deer</i>

01:00:59.238 --> 01:01:02.435
<i>- Ray</i>
<i>- A drop of golden sun</i>

01:01:02.708 --> 01:01:05.939
<i>- Me</i>
<i>- A name I call myself</i>

01:01:06.145 --> 01:01:09.205
<i>- Far</i>
<i>- A long long way to run</i>

01:01:09.448 --> 01:01:12.815
<i>- Sew</i>
<i>- A needle pulling thread</i>

01:01:13.118 --> 01:01:16.383
<i>- La</i>
<i>- A note to follow sew</i>

01:01:16.589 --> 01:01:19.581
<i>- Tea</i>
<i>- A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:01:19.792 --> 01:01:23.660
<i>That will bring us back to doe</i>

01:01:41.247 --> 01:01:47.516
<i>When you know the notes to sing</i>

01:01:48.087 --> 01:01:54.583
<i>You can sing most anything</i>

01:01:55.160 --> 01:01:58.323
<i>Doe</i>
<i>A deer, a female deer</i>

01:01:58.597 --> 01:02:02.124
<i>Ray</i>
<i>A drop of golden sun</i>

01:02:02.334 --> 01:02:05.792
<i>Me</i>
<i>A name I call myself</i>

01:02:06.038 --> 01:02:09.201
<i>Far</i>
<i>A long long way to run</i>

01:02:09.475 --> 01:02:12.638
<i>Sew</i>
<i>A needle pulling thread</i>

01:02:12.845 --> 01:02:16.042
<i>La</i>
<i>A note to follow sew</i>

01:02:16.649 --> 01:02:19.277
<i>Tea</i>
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

01:02:19.518 --> 01:02:23.477
<i>That will bring us back to</i>

01:02:23.689 --> 01:02:30.527
<i>So-do-la-fa-mi-do-re</i>

01:02:30.796 --> 01:02:35.290
<i>So-do-la-fa-ti</i>

01:02:35.534 --> 01:02:37.161
<i>La-so</i>

01:02:40.706 --> 01:02:46.508
<i>Ti-do</i>

01:02:46.712 --> 01:02:48.202
<i>So-do</i>

01:03:01.660 --> 01:03:04.754
The mountains are magnificent,
really magnificent.

01:03:04.997 --> 01:03:07.659
- I had them put up just for you.
- Oh?

01:03:07.933 --> 01:03:10.094
Even if it's to a height
of 10,000 feet...

01:03:10.369 --> 01:03:13.896
...Georg always believes in
"rising to the occasion."

01:03:14.173 --> 01:03:16.437
Improve the jokes
or I'll disinvite you.

01:03:17.042 --> 01:03:19.602
You didn't invite me.
I invited myself.

01:03:19.878 --> 01:03:22.403
- Naturally.
- You needed a chaperone...

01:03:22.681 --> 01:03:25.411
...and I needed a place
where the cuisine is superb...

01:03:25.684 --> 01:03:28.278
...the wine cellar unexcelled...

01:03:28.587 --> 01:03:31.181
...and the price perfect.

01:03:31.557 --> 01:03:33.388
Max, you are outrageous.

01:03:33.625 --> 01:03:37.618
Not at all.
I'm a very charming sponge.

01:03:40.265 --> 01:03:41.391
Listen.

01:03:43.736 --> 01:03:45.966
That's the Klopmann Monastery Choir.

01:03:48.974 --> 01:03:50.601
They're good.

01:03:51.643 --> 01:03:53.270
Very good.

01:03:54.079 --> 01:03:56.741
I must explore this area
in the next few days.

01:03:56.949 --> 01:04:00.407
Somewhere, a hungry singing group
is waiting for Max Detweiler...

01:04:00.652 --> 01:04:04.952
...to pluck it out and make it famous
at the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:04:05.157 --> 01:04:08.456
- They get fame, you get money.
- It's unfair, I admit it.

01:04:08.727 --> 01:04:13.096
But someday that'll be changed.
I shall get the fame too.

01:04:20.139 --> 01:04:22.300
Good heavens, what's this?

01:04:23.742 --> 01:04:26.074
It's nothing.
Just some local urchins.

01:04:41.293 --> 01:04:45.195
This really is exciting for me, Georg.
Being here with you.

01:04:46.031 --> 01:04:48.591
Trees, lakes,
you've seen them before.

01:04:48.867 --> 01:04:51.461
That is not what I mean,
and you know it.

01:04:51.703 --> 01:04:55.662
- You mean me? I'm exciting?
- Is that so impossible?

01:04:55.941 --> 01:04:58.967
No, just highly improbable.

01:04:59.211 --> 01:05:03.375
- There you go, running yourself down.
- Well, I'm a dangerous driver.

01:05:07.152 --> 01:05:10.849
You're much less of a riddle
when I see you here, Georg.

01:05:11.056 --> 01:05:13.889
- In my natural habitat?
- Yes, exactly.

01:05:14.193 --> 01:05:16.320
Are you saying that I'm more
at home...

01:05:16.562 --> 01:05:20.555
...among the birds and the flowers
and the wind that moves...

01:05:20.833 --> 01:05:22.994
...through the trees
like a restless sea?

01:05:23.235 --> 01:05:24.827
How poetic.

01:05:25.037 --> 01:05:26.902
Yes, it was rather, wasn't it?

01:05:28.040 --> 01:05:33.171
More at home here than in Vienna
in all your glittering salons...

01:05:33.378 --> 01:05:37.747
...gossiping gaily with bores I
detest, soaking myself in champagne...

01:05:38.050 --> 01:05:41.747
...stumbling about to waltzes
by Strausses I can't even remember?

01:05:42.054 --> 01:05:44.181
- Is that what you're saying?
- Yes.

01:05:44.423 --> 01:05:46.721
Now whatever gave you that idea?

01:05:50.095 --> 01:05:53.997
Oh, I do like it here, Georg.
It's so lovely and peaceful.

01:05:54.333 --> 01:05:56.267
How can you leave it so often?

01:05:56.535 --> 01:05:59.368
Oh, pretending to be madly active,
I suppose.

01:05:59.605 --> 01:06:02.870
Activity suggests a life
filled with purpose.

01:06:03.609 --> 01:06:05.873
Could it be running away
from memories?

01:06:09.081 --> 01:06:13.017
Or perhaps just searching
for a reason to stay.

01:06:13.685 --> 01:06:17.177
I hope that's why you've been
coming to Vienna so often.

01:06:17.856 --> 01:06:22.190
- Were there other distractions?
- I'd hardly call you a distraction.

01:06:22.427 --> 01:06:25.089
Well, what would you call me, Georg?

01:06:27.366 --> 01:06:28.628
Lovely...

01:06:29.635 --> 01:06:32.263
...charming, witty, graceful,
the perfect hostess...

01:06:32.471 --> 01:06:35.304
...and, you're going to hate me
for this...

01:06:35.741 --> 01:06:37.800
...in a way, my savior.

01:06:38.076 --> 01:06:39.907
Oh, how unromantic.

01:06:40.112 --> 01:06:42.444
I'd be an ungrateful wretch
if I didn't say...

01:06:42.714 --> 01:06:45.945
...that you brought some meaning back
into my life.

01:06:47.786 --> 01:06:50.550
I am amusing, I suppose.

01:06:50.789 --> 01:06:55.556
I have the finest couturier in Vienna
and a glittering circle of friends.

01:06:55.761 --> 01:06:58.889
- I do give some rather gay parties.
- Oh, yes.

01:06:59.131 --> 01:07:00.962
But take all that away...

01:07:01.166 --> 01:07:05.603
...and you have just wealthy,
unattached little me...

01:07:06.271 --> 01:07:08.671
...searching, just like you.

01:07:13.779 --> 01:07:15.474
More strudel, Herr Detweiler?

01:07:15.747 --> 01:07:17.271
- How many have I had?
- Two.

01:07:17.516 --> 01:07:19.450
Make it an uneven three.

01:07:22.754 --> 01:07:25.780
Still eating, Max?
Must be unhappy.

01:07:25.991 --> 01:07:29.950
That mixed quartet I've been trying
to steal away from Sol Hurok...

01:07:30.195 --> 01:07:32.857
- What happened?
...Sascha Petrie stole them first.

01:07:33.098 --> 01:07:34.360
I hate thieves.

01:07:34.633 --> 01:07:37.932
Max, you really must try
and learn to love yourself.

01:07:38.170 --> 01:07:40.502
I had to call Paris, Rome
and Stockholm.

01:07:40.772 --> 01:07:44.333
- On Georg's telephone, of course.
- How else could I afford it?

01:07:44.810 --> 01:07:49.941
I like rich people, the way they live
and how I live when I'm with them.

01:07:50.282 --> 01:07:52.273
I wonder where the children are.

01:07:52.684 --> 01:07:55.175
They must have heard
I was coming and hid.

01:07:55.454 --> 01:07:57.945
I was hoping they'd be here
to welcome you.

01:07:58.190 --> 01:08:02.684
Max, do step out of character for
a moment and try and be charming.

01:08:11.737 --> 01:08:13.136
Well?

01:08:14.039 --> 01:08:15.233
Well what?

01:08:15.474 --> 01:08:18.375
Have you made up his mind?
Do I hear wedding bells?

01:08:18.644 --> 01:08:20.635
- Pealing madly.
- Marvelous.

01:08:20.879 --> 01:08:23.643
- Not necessarily for me.
- What kind of talk's that?

01:08:23.849 --> 01:08:25.407
None-of-your-business talk.

01:08:25.717 --> 01:08:28.151
I'm terribly fond of him,
so don't toy with us.

01:08:28.420 --> 01:08:32.015
But I'm a child. I like toys.
So tell me everything.

01:08:32.324 --> 01:08:37.387
Come on. Tell me every teensy-weensy,
intimate, disgusting detail.

01:08:38.864 --> 01:08:42.994
Well, let's just say I have a feeling
I may be here on approval.

01:08:43.235 --> 01:08:46.261
- I approve of that. How can you miss?
- Far too easily.

01:08:46.538 --> 01:08:49.769
If I know you, darling,
and I do, you will find a way.

01:08:50.042 --> 01:08:52.533
- He's no ordinary man.
- No, he's rich.

01:08:52.778 --> 01:08:55.042
His wife's death gave him
a great heartache.

01:08:55.247 --> 01:08:58.375
And your husband's death
gave you a great fortune.

01:08:58.583 --> 01:09:00.551
Oh, Max, you really are a beast.

01:09:00.752 --> 01:09:04.779
You and Georg are like family.
That's why I want to see you married.

01:09:05.023 --> 01:09:08.584
We must keep all that lovely money
in the family.

01:09:24.876 --> 01:09:27.811
- What are you doing there?
- Oh, Captain von Trapp.

01:09:28.080 --> 01:09:30.105
I was just looking for...

01:09:30.982 --> 01:09:33.815
I didn't see, I mean,
I didn't know you were...

01:09:34.419 --> 01:09:36.114
Heil Hitler!

01:09:36.822 --> 01:09:38.312
Who are you?

01:09:38.590 --> 01:09:40.820
I have a telegram for Herr Detweiler.

01:09:41.093 --> 01:09:43.823
- I am Herr Detweiler.
- Yes, sir.

01:09:48.900 --> 01:09:51.494
You've delivered your telegram.
Now get out.

01:09:58.276 --> 01:10:01.677
- Georg, he's just a boy.
- Yes, and I'm just an Austrian.

01:10:01.913 --> 01:10:04.677
Things will happen.
Make sure they don't happen to you.

01:10:04.983 --> 01:10:07.645
Max! Don't you ever say that again.

01:10:07.919 --> 01:10:10.114
I have no political convictions.

01:10:10.355 --> 01:10:13.290
- Can I help it if other people do?
- You can help it.

01:10:14.426 --> 01:10:16.587
You must help it.

01:10:26.872 --> 01:10:28.464
Hello?

01:10:31.109 --> 01:10:33.873
You're far away. Where are you?

01:10:34.179 --> 01:10:38.047
In a world that's disappearing,
I'm afraid.

01:10:38.884 --> 01:10:42.479
Is there any way I could bring you
back to the world I'm in?

01:11:08.413 --> 01:11:10.904
- Father! Father!
- There's your father!

01:11:11.716 --> 01:11:14.344
Oh, captain, you're home!

01:11:22.727 --> 01:11:25.389
Come out of that water at once!

01:11:34.506 --> 01:11:36.701
Oh, you must be Baroness Schraeder.

01:11:42.013 --> 01:11:45.005
I'm soaked to the skin!

01:11:56.962 --> 01:11:58.361
Straight line!

01:12:13.044 --> 01:12:15.444
This is Baroness Schraeder.

01:12:18.049 --> 01:12:19.812
And these...

01:12:20.051 --> 01:12:21.643
...are my children.

01:12:22.754 --> 01:12:24.244
How do you do?

01:12:25.323 --> 01:12:30.056
Go inside, dry off, clean up, change
your clothes and report back here!

01:12:35.066 --> 01:12:37.159
Fräulein, you will stay here, please!

01:12:38.904 --> 01:12:42.465
I think I'd better go see
what Max is up to.

01:12:52.684 --> 01:12:54.447
Now, fräulein...

01:12:56.354 --> 01:12:58.413
...I want a truthful answer.

01:12:58.823 --> 01:13:00.290
Yes, captain.

01:13:00.592 --> 01:13:04.653
Is it possible,
or could I have just imagined it?

01:13:06.164 --> 01:13:10.658
Have my children, by any chance,
been climbing trees today?

01:13:11.136 --> 01:13:12.296
Yes, captain.

01:13:13.371 --> 01:13:14.702
I see.

01:13:15.273 --> 01:13:19.767
And where, may I ask,
did they get these...

01:13:20.045 --> 01:13:22.104
- Play clothes.
- Is that what they are?

01:13:22.314 --> 01:13:25.715
I made them from the drapes
that used to hang in my bedroom.

01:13:26.518 --> 01:13:28.645
- Drapes?
- They have plenty of wear left.

01:13:28.853 --> 01:13:30.787
We've been everywhere in them.

01:13:31.022 --> 01:13:35.482
Are you telling me that my children
have been roaming about Salzburg...

01:13:35.694 --> 01:13:39.061
...dressed up in nothing
but some old drapes?

01:13:39.297 --> 01:13:40.958
And having a marvelous time!

01:13:41.166 --> 01:13:44.397
- They have uniforms.
- Forgive me, straitjackets.

01:13:44.636 --> 01:13:47.400
They can't be children
if they worry about clothes...

01:13:47.672 --> 01:13:48.798
They don't complain.

01:13:49.040 --> 01:13:51.736
They don't dare.
They love you too much and fear...

01:13:51.977 --> 01:13:53.535
Don't discuss my children.

01:13:53.745 --> 01:13:55.679
You've got to hear, you're
never home...

01:13:55.880 --> 01:13:57.404
I don't want to hear more!

01:13:57.649 --> 01:14:00.140
I know you don't, but you've got to!

01:14:00.919 --> 01:14:03.080
- Liesl's not a child.
- Not one word...

01:14:03.355 --> 01:14:06.222
Soon she'll be a woman
and you won't even know her.

01:14:06.491 --> 01:14:09.551
Friedrich wants to be a man
but you're not here to show...

01:14:09.828 --> 01:14:11.159
Don't you dare tell me...

01:14:11.396 --> 01:14:14.661
Brigitta could tell you about him.
She notices everything.

01:14:14.899 --> 01:14:18.027
Kurt acts tough to hide the pain
when you ignore him...

01:14:18.236 --> 01:14:19.760
...the way you do all of them.

01:14:20.038 --> 01:14:22.438
Louisa, I don't know about yet.

01:14:22.707 --> 01:14:25.904
The little ones just want love.
Please, love them all.

01:14:26.177 --> 01:14:27.701
I don't care to hear more.

01:14:27.946 --> 01:14:32.042
- I am not finished yet, captain!
- Oh, yes, you are, captain!

01:14:33.585 --> 01:14:34.745
Fräulein.

01:14:36.054 --> 01:14:40.184
Now, you will pack
your things this minute...

01:14:40.392 --> 01:14:42.883
...and return to the abbey.

01:14:45.530 --> 01:14:46.861
What's that?

01:14:48.600 --> 01:14:49.624
It's singing.

01:14:50.268 --> 01:14:53.066
Yes, I realize it's singing.
But who is singing?

01:14:54.039 --> 01:14:55.597
The children.

01:14:58.476 --> 01:14:59.807
The children?

01:15:00.378 --> 01:15:03.108
I taught them something to sing
for the baroness.

01:15:08.753 --> 01:15:14.783
<i>My heart wants to sing</i>
<i>Every song it hears</i>

01:15:15.060 --> 01:15:17.620
<i>Every song that it hears</i>

01:15:17.896 --> 01:15:23.334
<i>My heart wants to beat like the wings</i>
<i>Of the birds that rise</i>

01:15:23.601 --> 01:15:26.729
<i>From the lake to the trees</i>

01:15:26.971 --> 01:15:28.404
<i>To the trees</i>

01:15:28.640 --> 01:15:33.577
<i>My heart wants to sigh</i>
<i>Like a chime that flies</i>

01:15:33.778 --> 01:15:38.408
<i>From a church on a breeze</i>

01:15:38.683 --> 01:15:42.585
<i>To laugh like a brook</i>
<i>When it trips and falls</i>

01:15:42.854 --> 01:15:45.789
<i>Over stones on its way</i>

01:15:46.091 --> 01:15:47.456
<i>On its way</i>

01:15:47.692 --> 01:15:52.129
<i>To sing through the night</i>

01:15:52.330 --> 01:15:57.996
<i>Like a lark who is learning to pray</i>

01:15:58.269 --> 01:16:02.763
<i>I go to the hills</i>

01:16:02.974 --> 01:16:09.209
<i>When my heart is lonely</i>

01:16:09.481 --> 01:16:13.178
<i>I know I will hear</i>

01:16:13.451 --> 01:16:19.219
<i>What I've heard before</i>

01:16:20.058 --> 01:16:24.290
<i>My heart will be blessed</i>

01:16:24.529 --> 01:16:31.492
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:16:32.370 --> 01:16:37.569
<i>And I'll sing...</i>

01:16:37.809 --> 01:16:45.909
<i>...once more</i>

01:17:19.184 --> 01:17:20.947
Edelweiss!

01:17:24.923 --> 01:17:28.086
You never told me how enchanting
your children are.

01:17:36.701 --> 01:17:38.259
Don't go away.

01:17:43.374 --> 01:17:44.773
Fräulein.

01:17:48.112 --> 01:17:49.306
I...

01:17:50.782 --> 01:17:53.580
...behaved badly. I apologize.

01:17:55.320 --> 01:17:58.915
I'm far too outspoken.
It's one of my worst faults.

01:17:59.324 --> 01:18:00.791
You were right.

01:18:03.261 --> 01:18:05.161
I don't know my children.

01:18:06.464 --> 01:18:10.594
There's still time, captain.
They want so much to be close to you.

01:18:10.935 --> 01:18:14.803
And you brought music back
into the house.

01:18:16.140 --> 01:18:17.573
I'd forgotten.

01:18:20.311 --> 01:18:21.642
Fräulein.

01:18:24.148 --> 01:18:25.410
I want you to stay.

01:18:29.420 --> 01:18:32.150
I ask you to stay.

01:18:33.992 --> 01:18:37.484
- If I could be of any help.
- You have already.

01:18:38.096 --> 01:18:39.154
More than you know.

01:18:58.883 --> 01:19:00.214
Marta.

01:19:00.952 --> 01:19:02.180
Curtain!

01:19:04.856 --> 01:19:08.189
<i>High on a hill was a lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:09.694 --> 01:19:12.959
<i>Loud was the voice</i>
<i>Of the lonely goatherd</i>

01:19:14.465 --> 01:19:17.730
<i>Folks in a town</i>
<i>That was quite remote heard</i>

01:19:19.304 --> 01:19:22.535
<i>Lusty and clear</i>
<i>From the goatherd's throat heard</i>

01:19:34.052 --> 01:19:36.919
Marta. Marta!

01:19:39.324 --> 01:19:41.315
Gretl, the prince!

01:19:43.061 --> 01:19:46.519
<i>A prince on the bridge</i>
<i>Of a castle moat heard</i>

01:19:47.999 --> 01:19:50.331
<i>Men on a road</i>
<i>With a load to tote heard</i>

01:19:52.837 --> 01:19:56.102
<i>Men in the midst</i>
<i>Of a table d'hôte heard</i>

01:19:57.442 --> 01:20:00.707
<i>Men drinking beer</i>
<i>With the foam afloat heard</i>

01:20:11.789 --> 01:20:14.917
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:20:16.561 --> 01:20:19.894
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:20:21.065 --> 01:20:24.466
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:20:25.970 --> 01:20:29.269
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:15.853 --> 01:21:19.118
<i>One little girl</i>
<i>In a pale pink coat heard</i>

01:21:20.658 --> 01:21:23.923
<i>She yodeled back</i>
<i>To the lonely goatherd</i>

01:21:25.263 --> 01:21:28.699
<i>Soon her mama</i>
<i>With a gleaming gloat heard</i>

01:21:30.168 --> 01:21:33.296
<i>What a duet for a girl and goatherd</i>

01:21:35.006 --> 01:21:36.633
<i>Happy are they</i>

01:21:39.610 --> 01:21:42.875
<i>Soon the duet will become a trio</i>

01:22:07.371 --> 01:22:08.963
- Bravo!
- Bravo!

01:22:09.173 --> 01:22:10.663
Very good!

01:22:12.477 --> 01:22:14.377
Wonderful!

01:22:14.979 --> 01:22:18.142
- Can we keep the puppets, Uncle Max?
- Yes, can we?

01:22:18.349 --> 01:22:20.374
Of course you may, my darlings.

01:22:20.585 --> 01:22:24.817
Why else did I tell Professor Kohner
to send the bill to your father?

01:22:28.559 --> 01:22:30.220
Well done, fräulein.

01:22:32.730 --> 01:22:34.698
I really am very much impressed.

01:22:34.899 --> 01:22:36.890
They're your children, captain.

01:22:44.108 --> 01:22:46.406
My dear, is there anything
you can't do?

01:22:46.677 --> 01:22:49.009
Well, I'm not sure
I'll make a good nun.

01:22:49.247 --> 01:22:52.341
If you have any problems,
I'd be happy to help you.

01:22:55.453 --> 01:22:56.886
Attention, everyone!

01:22:57.088 --> 01:23:00.546
I have an announcement to make.
Surprise! Surprise!

01:23:00.791 --> 01:23:03.089
Today, after a long
and desperate search...

01:23:03.361 --> 01:23:08.355
...I have found a most exciting
entry for the Salzburg Folk Festival.

01:23:08.566 --> 01:23:10.397
Congratulations, Max.

01:23:10.635 --> 01:23:13.604
And who will you
be exploiting this time?

01:23:15.406 --> 01:23:18.603
- The Saint Ignatius Choir?
- Guess again.

01:23:19.310 --> 01:23:23.246
Well, let me see now.
The Klopmann Choir?

01:23:23.481 --> 01:23:25.881
- No, no, no, no.
- No, no?

01:23:26.083 --> 01:23:27.277
Tell us.

01:23:27.485 --> 01:23:30.943
A singing group all in one family.
You'll never guess, Georg.

01:23:31.222 --> 01:23:34.123
What a charming idea!

01:23:34.325 --> 01:23:36.122
Whose family?

01:23:36.994 --> 01:23:38.621
Yours.

01:23:38.829 --> 01:23:41.161
They'll be the talk of the festival.

01:23:44.001 --> 01:23:46.993
- Well, now, what's so funny?
- You are, Max.

01:23:47.271 --> 01:23:50.399
You're expensive, but very funny.

01:23:51.142 --> 01:23:53.474
- They'll be a sensation!
- No, Max.

01:23:53.744 --> 01:23:55.939
It's a wonderful idea.
Fresh, original.

01:23:56.147 --> 01:24:00.948
Max! My children
do not sing in public.

01:24:01.619 --> 01:24:03.587
You can't blame me for trying.

01:24:03.788 --> 01:24:06.780
Children, who shall we hear
from next?

01:24:09.594 --> 01:24:10.754
Who?

01:24:16.934 --> 01:24:18.128
Yes.

01:24:21.005 --> 01:24:22.939
The vote is unanimous.

01:24:23.774 --> 01:24:25.332
You, captain.

01:24:25.610 --> 01:24:26.804
Me?

01:24:27.645 --> 01:24:29.943
- I don't understand.
- Please.

01:24:36.153 --> 01:24:38.280
No, no, no, no.

01:24:38.556 --> 01:24:40.615
I'm told that you were quite good.

01:24:40.825 --> 01:24:44.124
- That was a very, very long time ago.
- I remember, Father.

01:24:44.362 --> 01:24:47.229
- Play us something we know.
- Oh, please, Father.

01:24:50.167 --> 01:24:51.225
Well...

01:25:01.479 --> 01:25:03.640
- Why didn't you tell me?
- What?

01:25:03.914 --> 01:25:06.212
To bring along my harmonica.

01:25:08.552 --> 01:25:10.679
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:12.256 --> 01:25:14.554
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:15.660 --> 01:25:21.860
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:25:22.099 --> 01:25:25.159
<i>Small and white</i>

01:25:26.003 --> 01:25:29.370
<i>Clean and bright</i>

01:25:29.573 --> 01:25:32.406
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:25:32.610 --> 01:25:36.444
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:25:36.714 --> 01:25:39.012
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:25:39.283 --> 01:25:43.413
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:25:43.621 --> 01:25:49.958
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:25:50.928 --> 01:25:54.625
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:54.865 --> 01:25:57.459
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:25:58.135 --> 01:26:05.405
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:26:09.780 --> 01:26:12.977
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:13.284 --> 01:26:16.776
<i>- Edelweiss</i>
<i>- Edelweiss</i>

01:26:16.987 --> 01:26:23.392
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

01:26:23.627 --> 01:26:27.154
<i>- Small and white</i>
<i>- Small and white</i>

01:26:27.431 --> 01:26:30.889
<i>- Clean and bright</i>
<i>- Clean and bright</i>

01:26:31.102 --> 01:26:33.593
<i>You look happy...</i>

01:26:33.838 --> 01:26:37.467
<i>...to meet me</i>

01:26:37.942 --> 01:26:40.069
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

01:26:40.277 --> 01:26:44.441
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

01:26:44.682 --> 01:26:51.747
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

01:26:51.989 --> 01:26:55.618
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:55.860 --> 01:26:58.522
<i>Edelweiss</i>

01:26:59.130 --> 01:27:09.028
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

01:27:18.315 --> 01:27:21.978
Anytime you say the word, Georg,
you can be part of my new act:

01:27:22.186 --> 01:27:24.677
The von Trapp Family Singers.

01:27:25.790 --> 01:27:28.281
I have a wonderful idea, Georg.

01:27:28.526 --> 01:27:30.994
Let's really fill this house
with music.

01:27:31.228 --> 01:27:34.197
You must give a grand
and glorious party for me.

01:27:34.465 --> 01:27:37.161
- A party?
- Yes, Father, please!

01:27:37.368 --> 01:27:39.734
It's high time
I met all your friends...

01:27:40.037 --> 01:27:42.528
...and they met me.
Don't you agree?

01:27:42.807 --> 01:27:45.037
- I see what you mean.
- Oh, please!

01:27:45.309 --> 01:27:48.472
Children, it's bedtime.
Come now, say good night.

01:27:49.413 --> 01:27:50.710
Good night, Father.

01:27:50.915 --> 01:27:53.748
- Good night.
- Good night, Baroness Schraeder.

01:27:53.984 --> 01:27:55.542
Good night, Father.

01:27:58.522 --> 01:28:00.353
Good night, Uncle Max.

01:28:02.259 --> 01:28:05.422
It'll be my first party, Father!

01:28:37.962 --> 01:28:40.590
- Captain.
- Herr Zeller. Baroness Schraeder.

01:28:40.798 --> 01:28:43.926
- Good evening, Herr Zeller.
- Baroness.

01:28:45.236 --> 01:28:47.704
How do you do? Good evening.

01:29:08.325 --> 01:29:11.761
Did you notice the obvious
display of the Austrian flag?

01:29:18.836 --> 01:29:20.633
The women look so beautiful.

01:29:20.905 --> 01:29:22.236
I think they look ugly.

01:29:22.506 --> 01:29:24.337
You're just scared of them.

01:29:24.575 --> 01:29:26.805
Silly, only grown-up men fear women.

01:29:27.411 --> 01:29:30.972
- I think the men look beautiful.
- How would you know?

01:29:48.265 --> 01:29:50.290
Liesl, who are you dancing with?

01:29:50.501 --> 01:29:52.128
Nobody.

01:29:52.937 --> 01:29:54.837
Oh, yes, you are.

01:29:57.308 --> 01:29:58.798
May I have this dance?

01:29:59.009 --> 01:30:01.500
I'd be delighted, young man.

01:30:08.285 --> 01:30:10.947
Why didn't you tell me
you could dance?

01:30:11.188 --> 01:30:16.125
We feared you'd make us all dance.
The von Trapp Family Dancers.

01:30:20.531 --> 01:30:22.226
What are they playing?

01:30:22.466 --> 01:30:25.094
It's the Laendler.
An Austrian folk dance.

01:30:25.302 --> 01:30:28.465
- Show me.
- I haven't danced since I was little.

01:30:28.672 --> 01:30:30.640
You remember. Please?

01:30:30.908 --> 01:30:32.842
- Well...
- Please.

01:30:33.077 --> 01:30:35.307
All right. Come on over here.

01:30:35.813 --> 01:30:38.646
Now you bow and I curtsy.

01:30:39.583 --> 01:30:42.518
- Like this?
- Fine. Now we go for a little walk.

01:30:42.753 --> 01:30:45.415
One, two, three. One, two, three.

01:30:45.723 --> 01:30:50.319
One, two, three, step together.
Now, step hop, step hop.

01:30:50.561 --> 01:30:53.223
Now turn under. Not quite.

01:30:53.430 --> 01:30:57.389
This way. Hop step, hop.
And under.

01:30:58.068 --> 01:30:59.763
Kurt, we'll have to practice.

01:31:00.004 --> 01:31:01.494
Do allow me, will you?

01:32:29.793 --> 01:32:31.658
I don't remember anymore.

01:32:33.831 --> 01:32:36.026
- Your face is all red.
- Is it?

01:32:37.367 --> 01:32:39.460
I don't suppose I'm used to dancing.

01:32:42.172 --> 01:32:44.163
Why, that was beautifully done.

01:32:44.441 --> 01:32:46.341
What a lovely couple you make.

01:32:46.543 --> 01:32:48.670
It's time the children
said good night.

01:32:48.946 --> 01:32:50.277
We'll be in the hall.

01:32:50.514 --> 01:32:53.381
- We have something special prepared.
- Right!

01:32:53.684 --> 01:32:54.844
Yes, come on!

01:33:01.692 --> 01:33:04.024
All that needless worrying, Georg.

01:33:04.294 --> 01:33:07.320
You thought you wouldn't find
a friend at the party.

01:33:10.234 --> 01:33:13.829
- A bit chilly out tonight, isn't it?
- Oh, I don't know.

01:33:14.037 --> 01:33:16.062
It seemed rather warm to me.

01:33:20.244 --> 01:33:21.472
Ladies and gentlemen.

01:33:22.212 --> 01:33:26.308
The children of Captain von Trapp
wish to say good night to you.

01:33:40.430 --> 01:33:44.332
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

01:33:44.535 --> 01:33:48.266
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

01:33:48.539 --> 01:33:52.566
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

01:33:52.776 --> 01:33:55.210
<i>Is popping up to say "coo-coo"</i>

01:33:55.445 --> 01:33:57.106
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:57.381 --> 01:33:58.609
<i>Coo-coo</i>

01:33:58.849 --> 01:34:01.010
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

01:34:01.218 --> 01:34:02.583
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

01:34:02.853 --> 01:34:05.913
<i>To say goodbye</i>

01:34:06.123 --> 01:34:11.425
<i>To you</i>

01:34:14.631 --> 01:34:18.533
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

01:34:18.735 --> 01:34:22.603
<i>I hate to go</i>
<i>And leave this pretty sight</i>

01:34:29.880 --> 01:34:33.213
<i>So long, farewell,</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

01:34:33.884 --> 01:34:37.411
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

01:34:44.761 --> 01:34:48.561
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Au revoir, auf Wiedersehen</i>

01:34:48.832 --> 01:34:52.768
<i>I'd like to stay</i>
<i>And taste my first champagne</i>

01:34:53.003 --> 01:34:55.437
- Yes?
- No.

01:34:59.776 --> 01:35:03.439
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:03.780 --> 01:35:07.739
<i>I leave and heave a sigh</i>
<i>And say goodbye</i>

01:35:07.951 --> 01:35:11.944
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:35:14.992 --> 01:35:18.086
<i>I'm glad to go</i>

01:35:18.328 --> 01:35:21.195
<i>I cannot tell a lie</i>

01:35:21.531 --> 01:35:24.523
<i>I flit, I float</i>

01:35:24.801 --> 01:35:28.259
<i>I fleetly flee, I fly</i>

01:35:38.315 --> 01:35:44.049
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>

01:35:44.288 --> 01:35:48.019
<i>And so must I</i>

01:35:48.225 --> 01:35:50.625
<i>So long</i>

01:35:50.861 --> 01:35:53.421
<i>Farewell</i>

01:35:53.630 --> 01:35:59.034
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

01:35:59.303 --> 01:36:04.639
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:05.342 --> 01:36:10.905
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:11.148 --> 01:36:18.020
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:18.221 --> 01:36:26.720
<i>Goodbye</i>

01:36:31.735 --> 01:36:34.499
Extraordinary!
What they'd do at the festival.

01:36:34.738 --> 01:36:37.229
Young lady,
I must have a word with you.

01:36:38.241 --> 01:36:42.234
Georg, you won't let this girl
get away. She must join the party.

01:36:42.512 --> 01:36:44.912
- No, really l...
- Stop. Stop it now.

01:36:45.182 --> 01:36:48.117
- Georg, please.
- You can if you want to, fräulein.

01:36:48.352 --> 01:36:50.843
I insist.
You will be my dinner partner.

01:36:51.054 --> 01:36:52.954
This is business.
Franz...

01:36:53.223 --> 01:36:56.386
...set another place next to mine
for Fräulein Maria.

01:36:58.562 --> 01:37:01.292
- Whatever you say.
- It appears to be all arranged.

01:37:02.099 --> 01:37:03.964
- It does.
- I'm not suitably dressed.

01:37:05.035 --> 01:37:06.525
You can change. We'll wait.

01:37:10.140 --> 01:37:13.075
Captain, you must be very proud
of your youngsters.

01:37:13.276 --> 01:37:14.140
I am, thank you.

01:37:14.411 --> 01:37:18.973
Is there a more beautiful expression
of what is good in our country...

01:37:19.216 --> 01:37:22.652
...than the innocent voices
of our children?

01:37:23.053 --> 01:37:24.418
Oh, come now, baron.

01:37:24.654 --> 01:37:28.420
Would you have us believe that Austria
holds a monopoly on virtue?

01:37:29.326 --> 01:37:33.456
Herr Zeller, some of us prefer
Austrian voices raised in song...

01:37:33.663 --> 01:37:36.063
...to ugly German threats.

01:37:37.134 --> 01:37:40.763
The ostrich buries his head
in the sand...

01:37:40.971 --> 01:37:43.906
...and sometimes in the flag.

01:37:44.441 --> 01:37:48.639
Perhaps those who would warn you that
the Anschluss is coming, and it is...

01:37:48.912 --> 01:37:52.609
...would get further with you by setting
their words to music.

01:37:52.816 --> 01:37:57.480
If the Nazis take over Austria, you
will be the entire trumpet section.

01:37:57.788 --> 01:37:58.812
You flatter me.

01:37:59.856 --> 01:38:03.758
Oh, how clumsy of me.
I meant to accuse you.

01:38:11.501 --> 01:38:13.992
It's very kind of you
to offer to help me, baroness.

01:38:14.271 --> 01:38:15.829
I'm delighted, Maria.

01:38:16.306 --> 01:38:20.003
I really don't think I have anything
that would be appropriate.

01:38:20.477 --> 01:38:24.607
Now where is that lovely little thing
you were wearing the other evening?

01:38:24.848 --> 01:38:28.147
When the captain couldn't keep
his eyes off you.

01:38:31.521 --> 01:38:33.352
Couldn't keep his eyes off me?

01:38:34.691 --> 01:38:36.488
Come, my dear, we are women.

01:38:36.726 --> 01:38:40.127
Let's not pretend we don't know
when a man notices us.

01:38:40.363 --> 01:38:43.799
- Here we are.
- The captain notices everybody.

01:38:44.367 --> 01:38:46.801
There's no need to feel
so defensive, Maria.

01:38:47.037 --> 01:38:49.505
You are quite attractive, you know.

01:38:49.739 --> 01:38:53.368
The captain would hardly be a man
if he didn't notice you.

01:38:54.978 --> 01:38:57.344
Baroness, I hope you're joking.

01:38:57.814 --> 01:38:59.076
Not at all.

01:38:59.316 --> 01:39:00.908
I've never done a thing to...

01:39:01.184 --> 01:39:02.742
You don't have to, my dear.

01:39:03.386 --> 01:39:08.221
Nothing's more irresistible to a man
than a woman who's in love with him.

01:39:09.493 --> 01:39:11.927
- In love with him?
- Of course.

01:39:12.863 --> 01:39:16.264
What makes it so nice is
he thinks he's in love with you.

01:39:19.002 --> 01:39:20.594
But that's not true.

01:39:21.004 --> 01:39:24.496
Surely you've noticed the way
he looks into your eyes.

01:39:24.774 --> 01:39:29.677
And you know, you blushed in his arms
when you were dancing just now.

01:39:30.914 --> 01:39:32.609
Don't take it to heart.

01:39:32.883 --> 01:39:35.181
He'll get over it soon enough,
I think.

01:39:35.452 --> 01:39:37.420
Men do, you know.

01:39:38.421 --> 01:39:39.513
Then I should go.

01:39:40.857 --> 01:39:42.290
I mustn't stay here.

01:39:52.769 --> 01:39:56.205
- Is there something I can do to help?
- No, nothing.

01:39:57.974 --> 01:39:59.202
Yes.

01:40:00.210 --> 01:40:02.235
Don't say a word to the captain.

01:40:03.880 --> 01:40:07.441
No, I wouldn't dream of it.

01:40:14.224 --> 01:40:15.782
Goodbye, Maria.

01:40:16.593 --> 01:40:19.391
I'm sure you'll make a very fine nun.

01:40:49.426 --> 01:40:51.417
Champagne, darling.

01:40:51.828 --> 01:40:55.821
I feel like celebrating. Cheers.

01:41:01.304 --> 01:41:04.205
- You know something.
- Perhaps.

01:41:04.441 --> 01:41:08.969
If you're so clever, tell me how to
get fräulein to influence Georg.

01:41:09.212 --> 01:41:11.840
I want those children in the festival.

01:41:12.315 --> 01:41:14.613
Elsa, this is important to Austria.

01:41:14.818 --> 01:41:16.513
Wouldn't do you any harm either.

01:41:16.720 --> 01:41:18.312
I thought of that.

01:41:18.555 --> 01:41:21.023
Well, if it's a matter of influence...

01:41:21.224 --> 01:41:24.125
...maybe the one you have
to be talking to is me.

01:44:49.058 --> 01:44:51.288
- Two.
- Three.

01:44:51.560 --> 01:44:53.050
- Four.
- Five.

01:44:54.296 --> 01:44:56.321
- Six.
- Seven.

01:44:56.598 --> 01:44:58.225
Eight.

01:44:58.467 --> 01:45:00.298
- Four.
- Two.

01:45:01.403 --> 01:45:03.234
- Seven.
- Five.

01:45:03.472 --> 01:45:05.667
- Two.
- Six.

01:45:10.312 --> 01:45:12.337
Isn't this fun?

01:45:13.749 --> 01:45:16.081
- Four.
- I'm number five.

01:45:16.351 --> 01:45:18.512
- Oh, yes.
- Eight.

01:45:18.821 --> 01:45:21.187
- Two.
- Four.

01:45:21.590 --> 01:45:22.818
Six.

01:45:25.294 --> 01:45:26.522
Two.

01:45:27.663 --> 01:45:30.632
Baroness Schraeder, do you mind
if we stop now? We're tired.

01:45:30.866 --> 01:45:32.834
Whatever you want, dear.

01:45:33.102 --> 01:45:35.093
We'll do it again tomorrow.

01:45:45.280 --> 01:45:47.441
The country's so restful, isn't it?

01:45:48.484 --> 01:45:50.111
Have some lemonade.

01:45:51.353 --> 01:45:52.786
There must be an easier way.

01:45:54.189 --> 01:45:57.454
I get a fiendish delight thinking
of you as the mother of seven.

01:45:58.393 --> 01:46:00.224
How do you plan to do it?

01:46:00.496 --> 01:46:02.521
Darling, haven't you ever heard...

01:46:02.798 --> 01:46:05.892
...of a delightful little thing
called boarding school?

01:46:07.035 --> 01:46:09.299
Baroness Machiavelli.

01:46:10.639 --> 01:46:12.630
Uncle Max, where's Father?

01:46:12.908 --> 01:46:14.705
I think he's in the house.

01:46:14.910 --> 01:46:17.470
What's the matter
with all you gloomy pussies?

01:46:17.713 --> 01:46:20.511
- Nothing.
- I know. Let's have a rehearsal.

01:46:20.716 --> 01:46:21.614
What for?

01:46:21.817 --> 01:46:24.308
Let's make believe we're on-stage
at the festival.

01:46:24.520 --> 01:46:28.388
- I don't feel like singing.
- Not without Fräulein Maria.

01:46:28.657 --> 01:46:31.057
Liesl, get the guitar.
Come on, Marta.

01:46:31.260 --> 01:46:34.229
Everybody into the group.
Get in your places.

01:46:34.496 --> 01:46:37.260
Now be cheerful, right?
Give us the key, Liesl.

01:46:39.168 --> 01:46:41.830
Now, impress me.

01:46:45.841 --> 01:46:47.172
Gretl, why don't you sing?

01:46:47.442 --> 01:46:49.910
I can't. I've got a sore finger.

01:46:50.946 --> 01:46:54.006
But you sang so beautifully
the night of the party.

01:46:54.216 --> 01:46:56.548
Come on, all of you.
Try something you know.

01:46:56.785 --> 01:46:58.275
Enjoy it. Be cheerful.

01:46:58.554 --> 01:47:00.181
All right, Liesl.

01:47:02.124 --> 01:47:07.528
<i>The hills are alive</i>

01:47:07.763 --> 01:47:15.431
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:16.638 --> 01:47:21.701
<i>With songs they have sung</i>

01:47:21.944 --> 01:47:29.783
<i>For a thousand years</i>

01:47:30.485 --> 01:47:35.889
<i>The hills fill my heart</i>

01:47:36.124 --> 01:47:43.826
<i>With the sound of music</i>

01:47:44.166 --> 01:47:46.794
They wanted to sing for me,
bless their hearts.

01:47:47.102 --> 01:47:49.002
That's lovely, lovely.
Don't stop.

01:47:53.008 --> 01:47:56.910
- Something long and cool, Georg?
- No, thank you, darling.

01:47:57.312 --> 01:47:59.746
- Father?
- Yes, Brigitta?

01:48:00.182 --> 01:48:02.446
Is it true Fräulein Maria
isn't coming back?

01:48:02.751 --> 01:48:05.845
Yes, I suppose it's true.
What have we got here?

01:48:06.154 --> 01:48:10.853
- Pink lemonade.
- Laced with lemonade.

01:48:11.593 --> 01:48:13.117
I don't believe it, Father.

01:48:14.496 --> 01:48:16.521
- What?
- About Fräulein Maria.

01:48:16.932 --> 01:48:18.160
Oh, Fräulein Maria!

01:48:18.467 --> 01:48:21.925
Didn't I tell you what her note said?
I'm sure I did.

01:48:22.671 --> 01:48:25.162
She said she missed her life
at the abbey.

01:48:25.440 --> 01:48:27.601
She had to leave us.

01:48:27.843 --> 01:48:29.435
And that's all there is to it.

01:48:31.146 --> 01:48:33.842
I think I'm brave enough to try
some of that.

01:48:34.049 --> 01:48:36.779
- She didn't even say goodbye.
- She did in her note.

01:48:37.052 --> 01:48:38.849
That isn't the same thing.

01:48:39.154 --> 01:48:40.781
Not too sweet, not too sour.

01:48:41.523 --> 01:48:43.514
Just too pink.

01:48:44.960 --> 01:48:48.054
Father, who is our new governess
going to be?

01:48:54.703 --> 01:48:55.795
Well...

01:48:58.140 --> 01:49:03.373
...you're not going to have
a governess anymore.

01:49:03.712 --> 01:49:06.374
- We're not?
- No.

01:49:08.583 --> 01:49:10.710
You're going to have a new mother.

01:49:11.820 --> 01:49:13.845
A new mother?

01:49:14.690 --> 01:49:17.818
We talked about it last night.
It's all settled.

01:49:18.026 --> 01:49:20.722
And we're all going to be very happy.

01:49:53.729 --> 01:49:56.197
Well, all right, all right.
Run off and play.

01:50:28.163 --> 01:50:29.130
Yes, my children?

01:50:29.331 --> 01:50:31.731
- My name is Liesl.
- Yes, Liesl?

01:50:32.234 --> 01:50:36.170
We, my brothers and sisters,
want to see Fräulein Maria.

01:50:37.339 --> 01:50:39.330
Fräulein Maria?

01:50:40.108 --> 01:50:42.076
Oh, Maria.

01:50:43.979 --> 01:50:45.810
Come in, please.

01:50:49.684 --> 01:50:51.242
Wait here.

01:51:02.197 --> 01:51:05.360
I'm Sister Margaretta. I understand
you inquired about Maria.

01:51:05.634 --> 01:51:08.125
We have to see her.
Will you tell her we're here?

01:51:08.370 --> 01:51:10.964
- I'm afraid I can't do that.
- But you've got to!

01:51:11.273 --> 01:51:13.332
- She's our governess.
- We want her back.

01:51:13.542 --> 01:51:15.442
She didn't even say goodbye.

01:51:15.677 --> 01:51:17.440
All we want to do is talk to her.

01:51:18.213 --> 01:51:21.114
I'm very sorry,
but Maria is in seclusion.

01:51:21.349 --> 01:51:24.443
- She hasn't been seeing anyone.
- She'll see us.

01:51:24.686 --> 01:51:27.177
I want to show her my finger.

01:51:27.389 --> 01:51:29.289
Some other time, dear.

01:51:29.558 --> 01:51:30.855
I'll tell her you were here.

01:51:31.126 --> 01:51:34.186
- It was sweet of you to call.
- We have to speak to her!

01:51:34.830 --> 01:51:37.958
Run along, children.
Run along home.

01:51:38.166 --> 01:51:39.793
I'm sure she'd like to see us.

01:51:40.068 --> 01:51:42.332
Sister Margaretta, please.

01:51:42.571 --> 01:51:46.302
- Goodbye, children.
- Sister Margaretta, may we, please?

01:51:49.077 --> 01:51:50.806
What was that about, Sister?

01:51:51.046 --> 01:51:53.241
The von Trapp children,
Reverend Mother.

01:51:53.482 --> 01:51:55.916
They want to see Maria.

01:51:56.184 --> 01:51:58.482
Has she spoken yet?
Has she told you anything?

01:51:58.753 --> 01:52:02.746
She doesn't say a word,
Reverend Mother, except in prayer.

01:52:03.024 --> 01:52:04.013
Poor child.

01:52:04.226 --> 01:52:07.195
It's strange.
She seems happy to be back here...

01:52:07.429 --> 01:52:10.728
...and yet she's unhappy too.

01:52:12.000 --> 01:52:15.060
Perhaps I have been wrong
in leaving her alone so long.

01:52:15.337 --> 01:52:18.033
Bring her to me,
even if she's not yet ready.

01:52:18.240 --> 01:52:19.901
Yes, Reverend Mother.

01:52:25.413 --> 01:52:28.905
Sister Augusta, take our new postulant
to the robing room.

01:52:29.918 --> 01:52:32.182
God bless you, my daughter.

01:52:38.393 --> 01:52:40.122
Yes, bring her in.

01:52:49.137 --> 01:52:51.401
You've been unhappy. I'm sorry.

01:52:53.441 --> 01:52:54.635
Reverend Mother.

01:52:54.976 --> 01:52:57.604
Why did they send you back to us?

01:52:58.446 --> 01:53:00.414
They didn't send me back.
I left.

01:53:02.918 --> 01:53:04.476
Sit down, Maria.

01:53:04.986 --> 01:53:06.783
Tell me what happened.

01:53:11.993 --> 01:53:13.324
I was frightened.

01:53:13.595 --> 01:53:18.055
- Frightened? Were they unkind to you.
- Oh, no!

01:53:18.300 --> 01:53:21.997
No, I was confused. I felt...

01:53:23.471 --> 01:53:25.564
I've never felt that way before.

01:53:25.807 --> 01:53:29.573
I couldn't stay. I knew that here
I'd be away from it. I'd be safe.

01:53:29.811 --> 01:53:34.510
Maria, our abbey is not to be used
as an escape.

01:53:34.783 --> 01:53:37.013
What is it you can't face?

01:53:38.987 --> 01:53:40.420
I can't face him again.

01:53:41.256 --> 01:53:42.780
Him?

01:53:44.359 --> 01:53:46.418
Thank you, Sister Margaretta.

01:53:56.037 --> 01:53:57.664
Captain von Trapp?

01:54:03.111 --> 01:54:05.807
- Are you in love with him?
- I don't know!

01:54:06.047 --> 01:54:07.514
I don't know. I...

01:54:08.049 --> 01:54:11.883
The baroness said I was.
She said that he was in love with me.

01:54:12.153 --> 01:54:14.815
But I didn't want to believe it.

01:54:15.890 --> 01:54:18.188
There were times we looked
at each other.

01:54:18.393 --> 01:54:19.951
I could hardly breathe.

01:54:20.328 --> 01:54:23.024
- Did you let him see your feelings?
- I don't know.

01:54:23.632 --> 01:54:26.294
That's what's torturing me.
I was on God's errand.

01:54:26.501 --> 01:54:31.495
To have asked for his love would have
been wrong. I just couldn't stay.

01:54:33.675 --> 01:54:36.473
I'm ready at this moment
to take my vows.

01:54:37.345 --> 01:54:40.405
- Please help me.
- Maria.

01:54:41.983 --> 01:54:46.682
The love of a man and a woman is holy.
You have a great capacity to love.

01:54:46.921 --> 01:54:49.856
You must find out how God
wants you to spend your love.

01:54:50.158 --> 01:54:53.992
But I pledged my life to God.
I pledged my life to his service.

01:54:54.195 --> 01:54:58.564
My daughter, if you love this man,
it doesn't mean you love God less.

01:55:00.235 --> 01:55:02.100
No.

01:55:02.337 --> 01:55:04.202
You must find out.

01:55:05.940 --> 01:55:08.431
You must go back.

01:55:08.710 --> 01:55:10.678
You can't ask me to do that.

01:55:10.879 --> 01:55:13.370
- Please let me stay. I beg...
- Maria.

01:55:13.581 --> 01:55:17.540
These walls were not built
to shut out problems.

01:55:17.752 --> 01:55:19.344
You have to face them.

01:55:19.921 --> 01:55:23.186
You have to live the life
you were born to live.

01:55:29.064 --> 01:55:33.364
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:33.601 --> 01:55:37.367
<i>Search high and low</i>

01:55:37.605 --> 01:55:42.372
<i>Follow every byway</i>

01:55:42.610 --> 01:55:46.876
<i>Every path you know</i>

01:55:47.315 --> 01:55:51.775
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:55:52.053 --> 01:55:56.387
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:55:56.624 --> 01:56:00.993
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:01.262 --> 01:56:05.596
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:05.800 --> 01:56:08.894
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:09.137 --> 01:56:13.972
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:14.743 --> 01:56:18.144
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:56:18.413 --> 01:56:24.818
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:56:25.120 --> 01:56:29.420
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:56:29.657 --> 01:56:33.991
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:56:34.262 --> 01:56:38.824
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:56:39.033 --> 01:56:47.441
<i>Till you find your dream</i>

01:56:48.543 --> 01:56:52.035
<i>A dream that will need</i>

01:56:52.347 --> 01:56:57.876
<i>All the love you can give</i>

01:56:58.153 --> 01:57:01.645
<i>Every day of your life</i>

01:57:01.890 --> 01:57:08.318
<i>For as long as you live</i>

01:57:08.563 --> 01:57:13.000
<i>Climb every mountain</i>

01:57:13.234 --> 01:57:17.170
<i>Ford every stream</i>

01:57:17.839 --> 01:57:22.469
<i>Follow every rainbow</i>

01:57:22.877 --> 01:57:26.973
<i>Till you find...</i>

01:57:27.215 --> 01:57:37.216
<i>...your dream</i>

01:57:39.761 --> 01:57:43.322
Now, it's not like my children
to be secretive.

01:57:43.565 --> 01:57:45.658
We're not being secretive, Father.

01:57:47.335 --> 01:57:50.668
And it's not like my children
to be late for dinner.

01:57:50.939 --> 01:57:54.375
- We lost track of the time.
- I see.

01:57:55.176 --> 01:57:58.577
Who's going to be the first one
to tell me the truth? Friedrich.

01:57:58.847 --> 01:58:00.906
Brigitta. Liesl.

01:58:02.283 --> 01:58:04.513
Where do you think we were, Father?

01:58:11.092 --> 01:58:15.051
If you don't believe us, you must have
some idea of where you think we were.

01:58:18.633 --> 01:58:20.430
- Marta.
- Yes, Father.

01:58:20.635 --> 01:58:21.897
You tell me.

01:58:23.238 --> 01:58:26.867
Friedrich told you, Father.
We were berry picking.

01:58:27.709 --> 01:58:32.373
- I forgot! You were berry picking.
- Yes, we love berry picking.

01:58:32.614 --> 01:58:33.706
All afternoon?

01:58:33.948 --> 01:58:35.677
- We picked thousands.
- Thousands?

01:58:35.884 --> 01:58:38.785
- They were all over the place.
- What kind of berries?

01:58:39.053 --> 01:58:42.318
- Blueberries, sir.
- Blueberries.

01:58:44.259 --> 01:58:47.626
It's too early for blueberries.

01:58:49.130 --> 01:58:51.223
- They were strawberries.
- Strawberries?

01:58:51.933 --> 01:58:54.629
It's been so cold lately,
they turned blue.

01:59:00.475 --> 01:59:02.636
Very well. Show me the berries.

01:59:03.912 --> 01:59:05.106
- We...
- Well...

01:59:05.346 --> 01:59:08.110
- Show me the berries you picked.
- We don't have them.

01:59:08.349 --> 01:59:10.613
You don't have them?
What happened to them?

01:59:10.852 --> 01:59:13.650
- We...
- We ate them.

01:59:13.855 --> 01:59:16.449
- You ate them?
- Yes!

01:59:16.658 --> 01:59:18.250
- They were so good.
- Delicious.

01:59:18.493 --> 01:59:19.687
Very well.

01:59:19.961 --> 01:59:25.092
Since you've obviously stuffed
yourselves on thousands of berries...

01:59:25.333 --> 01:59:29.269
...you can't be hungry anymore,
so I'll have to tell Frau Schmidt...

01:59:29.504 --> 01:59:32.371
...to skip your dinner.

01:59:41.549 --> 01:59:44.347
It's your fault.
We should have told him the truth.

01:59:44.619 --> 01:59:46.587
And made him boiling mad at us?

01:59:46.788 --> 01:59:48.722
It's better than starving to death.

01:59:48.957 --> 01:59:51.824
We didn't do anything wrong.
We just wanted to see her.

01:59:53.127 --> 01:59:56.221
My stomach's making noises.

01:59:56.664 --> 01:59:59.497
The least they could have done
was to let us say hello.

02:00:00.635 --> 02:00:04.537
- I wonder what grass tastes like.
- I feel awful.

02:00:04.973 --> 02:00:09.239
When Fräulein Maria wanted to feel
better she used to sing that song.

02:00:09.844 --> 02:00:11.311
Let's try it.

02:00:11.546 --> 02:00:14.208
<i>Raindrops on roses</i>

02:00:14.515 --> 02:00:18.542
<i>And whiskers on kittens</i>

02:00:19.387 --> 02:00:21.981
<i>Bright copper kettles</i>

02:00:22.190 --> 02:00:25.250
<i>And warm woolen mittens</i>

02:00:26.594 --> 02:00:32.555
<i>Brown paper packages</i>
<i>Tied up with strings</i>

02:00:32.834 --> 02:00:38.830
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:00:39.073 --> 02:00:41.098
Why don't I feel better?

02:00:42.276 --> 02:00:44.574
<i>Girls in white dresses</i>

02:00:44.846 --> 02:00:47.940
<i>With blue satin sashes</i>

02:00:48.216 --> 02:00:53.848
<i>Snowflakes that stay</i>
<i>On my nose and eyelashes</i>

02:00:54.222 --> 02:00:57.385
- <i>Silver white winters...</i>
- Fräulein Maria's back!

02:00:57.592 --> 02:00:58.889
<i>...that melt into springs</i>

02:00:59.293 --> 02:01:02.558
<i>These are a few of my favorite things</i>

02:01:02.797 --> 02:01:05.891
<i>When the dog bites</i>
<i>When the bee stings</i>

02:01:06.100 --> 02:01:08.227
<i>When I'm feeling sad</i>

02:01:08.736 --> 02:01:11.705
<i>I simply remember my favorite things</i>

02:01:11.973 --> 02:01:14.237
<i>And then I don't feel</i>

02:01:14.442 --> 02:01:21.211
<i>So bad</i>

02:01:21.449 --> 02:01:24.475
- Children, I'm so glad to see you.
- We missed you.

02:01:24.719 --> 02:01:25.708
I missed you.

02:01:25.987 --> 02:01:28.114
- Kurt, how are you?
- Hungry.

02:01:29.657 --> 02:01:32.285
- What happened to your finger?
- It got caught.

02:01:32.560 --> 02:01:34.721
- Caught in what?
- Friedrich's teeth.

02:01:35.963 --> 02:01:38.124
- Liesl, you all right?
- Just fair.

02:01:38.332 --> 02:01:41.324
- Any telegrams been delivered lately?
- None at all.

02:01:41.569 --> 02:01:45.005
But I'm learning to accept it.
I'll be glad when school begins.

02:01:45.306 --> 02:01:50.005
Liesl, you can't use school to escape
your problems. You have to face them.

02:01:50.244 --> 02:01:51.677
I have so much to tell you.

02:01:51.946 --> 02:01:53.937
We have things to tell you too.

02:01:54.282 --> 02:01:57.979
The most important thing is
that Father is going to be married.

02:01:58.186 --> 02:01:59.244
Married?

02:01:59.587 --> 02:02:01.612
Yes, to Baroness Schraeder.

02:02:09.530 --> 02:02:11.088
Oh, I see.

02:02:12.934 --> 02:02:16.301
Father, look!
Fräulein Maria's back!

02:02:16.537 --> 02:02:18.596
Fräulein Maria's back from the abbey.

02:02:20.808 --> 02:02:21.866
Good evening, captain.

02:02:23.344 --> 02:02:24.641
Good evening.

02:02:27.181 --> 02:02:29.012
Everyone inside for dinner.

02:02:29.317 --> 02:02:30.875
Dinner!

02:02:40.228 --> 02:02:44.961
You left without saying goodbye.
Even to the children.

02:02:45.967 --> 02:02:47.491
It was wrong of me. Forgive me.

02:02:49.537 --> 02:02:50.697
Why did you?

02:02:50.905 --> 02:02:53.738
Please don't ask me.
The reason no longer exists.

02:02:54.909 --> 02:02:58.003
Fräulein Maria, you've returned.

02:02:59.247 --> 02:03:01.044
Isn't it wonderful, Georg?

02:03:04.352 --> 02:03:06.582
I wish you every happiness,
baroness.

02:03:06.821 --> 02:03:09.517
You too, captain.
The children say you're to marry.

02:03:09.757 --> 02:03:10.883
Thank you, my dear.

02:03:13.427 --> 02:03:16.988
You are back to stay?

02:03:19.066 --> 02:03:22.399
Only until arrangements can be made
for another governess.

02:04:18.092 --> 02:04:19.719
There you are.

02:04:34.108 --> 02:04:36.576
I must speak to cook
about the schnitzel.

02:04:36.844 --> 02:04:40.143
It is entirely too delicious
for my figure.

02:04:40.581 --> 02:04:43.516
And it makes you much too quiet
at the dinner table.

02:04:43.784 --> 02:04:45.775
Or was it the wine?

02:04:46.020 --> 02:04:47.851
Undoubtedly the wine.

02:04:50.424 --> 02:04:52.688
You have no idea
the trouble I'm having...

02:04:52.960 --> 02:04:55.690
...trying to decide on
a wedding present for you.

02:04:55.997 --> 02:04:58.158
Oh, I know. I'm enough.

02:04:58.432 --> 02:05:02.027
But I do want you to have
some little trifle for the occasion.

02:05:02.270 --> 02:05:04.602
At first I thought
of a fountain pen...

02:05:04.839 --> 02:05:07.103
...but you've already got one.

02:05:07.375 --> 02:05:10.310
Then I thought perhaps a villa
in the south of France...

02:05:10.544 --> 02:05:13.206
...but they are so difficult
to gift-wrap.

02:05:13.481 --> 02:05:15.881
Oh, Georg, how do you
feel about yachts?

02:05:16.183 --> 02:05:18.447
A long, sleek one
for the Mediterranean...

02:05:18.686 --> 02:05:21.450
...or a tiny one
for your bathtub, huh?

02:05:23.624 --> 02:05:25.649
- Elsa.
- Where to go on our honeymoon?

02:05:25.893 --> 02:05:27.485
Now, that's a real problem.

02:05:27.695 --> 02:05:31.062
A trip around the world
would be lovely. And then I said:

02:05:31.365 --> 02:05:34.198
"Oh, Elsa, there must be
someplace better to go."

02:05:34.468 --> 02:05:36.902
- But don't worry, darling, I'll...
- Elsa.

02:05:37.571 --> 02:05:38.833
Yes, Georg.

02:05:39.840 --> 02:05:41.171
It's no use...

02:05:42.376 --> 02:05:43.741
...you and I.

02:05:45.313 --> 02:05:48.544
I'm being dishonest to both of us...

02:05:49.884 --> 02:05:51.545
...and utterly unfair to you.

02:05:56.824 --> 02:05:59.554
- When two people talk of marriage...
- No, don't.

02:06:00.428 --> 02:06:02.521
Don't say another word, please.

02:06:05.833 --> 02:06:10.861
You see, there are other things
I've been thinking of.

02:06:11.772 --> 02:06:16.505
Fond as I am of you, I really don't
think you're the right man for me.

02:06:19.046 --> 02:06:21.537
You're much too independent.

02:06:21.849 --> 02:06:26.548
And I need someone
who needs me desperately...

02:06:26.854 --> 02:06:29.846
...or at least needs
my money desperately.

02:06:32.026 --> 02:06:36.929
I've enjoyed every moment we've had
together and I do thank you for that.

02:06:39.700 --> 02:06:41.600
Now, if you'll forgive me...

02:06:41.802 --> 02:06:43.861
...I'll go inside,
pack my little bags...

02:06:44.105 --> 02:06:46.596
...and return to Vienna
where I belong.

02:06:51.979 --> 02:06:53.810
And somewhere out there...

02:06:54.115 --> 02:06:58.484
...is a young lady who, I think...

02:06:58.753 --> 02:06:59.981
...will never be a nun.

02:07:12.133 --> 02:07:14.465
Auf Wiedersehen, darling.

02:07:40.194 --> 02:07:41.354
Hello.

02:07:47.168 --> 02:07:50.763
I thought I just might find you here.

02:07:54.942 --> 02:07:57.206
Was there something you wanted?

02:07:57.645 --> 02:08:00.773
No, no, no. Sit down, please.

02:08:01.715 --> 02:08:03.046
Please.

02:08:08.189 --> 02:08:09.520
May I?

02:08:21.902 --> 02:08:26.635
You know, I was thinking
and I was wondering two things:

02:08:27.808 --> 02:08:32.040
Why did you run away to the abbey?

02:08:32.880 --> 02:08:37.544
And what was it
that made you come back?

02:08:39.220 --> 02:08:43.680
Well, I had an obligation
to fulfill...

02:08:43.891 --> 02:08:46.018
...and I came back to fulfill it.

02:08:46.660 --> 02:08:48.093
Is that all?

02:08:49.430 --> 02:08:51.591
And I missed the children.

02:08:51.932 --> 02:08:53.092
Yes.

02:08:54.368 --> 02:08:57.269
- Only the children?
- No. Yes.

02:08:57.505 --> 02:09:01.339
- Isn't it right that I missed them?
- Oh, yes. Yes, of course.

02:09:01.542 --> 02:09:04.170
I was only hoping that perhaps you...

02:09:05.279 --> 02:09:07.042
Perhaps you might...

02:09:08.782 --> 02:09:10.010
Yes?

02:09:11.785 --> 02:09:17.087
Well, nothing was the same
when you were away...

02:09:17.858 --> 02:09:21.089
...and it'll be all wrong again
after you leave...

02:09:21.295 --> 02:09:25.959
...and I just thought perhaps
you might change your mind.

02:09:30.037 --> 02:09:34.269
Well, I'm sure the baroness will be
able to make things fine for you.

02:09:34.542 --> 02:09:35.873
Maria...

02:09:37.978 --> 02:09:41.470
- There isn't going to be any baroness.
- There isn't?

02:09:43.884 --> 02:09:45.249
No.

02:09:45.553 --> 02:09:47.316
I don't understand.

02:09:49.723 --> 02:09:53.819
Well, we've called off our engagement,
you see, and...

02:09:54.094 --> 02:09:57.552
- Oh, I'm sorry.
- Yes. You are?

02:09:58.732 --> 02:10:00.825
- You did?
- Yes.

02:10:01.969 --> 02:10:06.497
Well, you can't marry someone
when you're...

02:10:09.076 --> 02:10:11.135
...in love with someone else...

02:10:14.515 --> 02:10:15.948
...can you?

02:10:50.818 --> 02:10:53.116
The Reverend Mother always says:

02:10:53.354 --> 02:10:56.790
"When the Lord closes a door,
somewhere He opens a window."

02:11:05.199 --> 02:11:08.225
What else does
the Reverend Mother say?

02:11:09.169 --> 02:11:11.569
That you have to look for your life.

02:11:13.240 --> 02:11:15.800
Is that why you came back?

02:11:19.847 --> 02:11:21.314
And have you found it...

02:11:22.316 --> 02:11:23.476
...Maria?

02:11:25.252 --> 02:11:27.243
I think I have.

02:11:29.990 --> 02:11:31.389
I know I have.

02:11:33.894 --> 02:11:35.555
I love you.

02:11:39.533 --> 02:11:41.398
Oh, can this be happening to me?

02:11:44.772 --> 02:11:50.176
<i>Perhaps I had a wicked childhood</i>

02:11:51.679 --> 02:11:56.912
<i>Perhaps I had a miserable youth</i>

02:11:58.786 --> 02:12:04.725
<i>But somewhere</i>
<i>In my wicked, miserable past</i>

02:12:05.225 --> 02:12:11.027
<i>There must have been a moment of truth</i>

02:12:11.965 --> 02:12:18.734
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:12:19.473 --> 02:12:25.469
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:12:26.113 --> 02:12:32.916
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:12:33.787 --> 02:12:41.421
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:12:42.663 --> 02:12:45.632
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:12:46.767 --> 02:12:50.635
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:12:51.472 --> 02:13:00.346
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:01.915 --> 02:13:11.415
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:13:12.292 --> 02:13:17.127
Do you know when I first
started loving you?

02:13:17.531 --> 02:13:21.433
That night at dinner, when you sat
on that ridiculous pine cone.

02:13:21.668 --> 02:13:22.965
What?

02:13:24.304 --> 02:13:27.762
I knew the first time you blew
that silly whistle.

02:13:28.675 --> 02:13:30.666
Oh, my love.

02:13:34.448 --> 02:13:42.355
<i>For here you are</i>
<i>Standing there loving me</i>

02:13:44.324 --> 02:13:50.160
<i>Whether or not you should</i>

02:13:51.532 --> 02:13:58.563
<i>So somewhere in my youth or childhood</i>

02:13:59.373 --> 02:14:07.075
<i>I must have done something good</i>

02:14:08.248 --> 02:14:11.740
<i>Nothing comes from nothing</i>

02:14:12.486 --> 02:14:15.512
<i>Nothing ever could</i>

02:14:15.756 --> 02:14:21.558
<i>So somewhere in my youth...</i>

02:14:21.829 --> 02:14:24.059
<i>...or childhood</i>

02:14:27.167 --> 02:14:33.697
<i>I must have done something</i>

02:14:35.742 --> 02:14:48.382
<i>Something good</i>

02:14:55.095 --> 02:14:56.619
Maria.

02:14:58.465 --> 02:15:03.061
Is there anyone I should go to,
to ask permission to marry you?

02:15:06.974 --> 02:15:09.534
- Why don't we ask...
- The children?

02:16:58.051 --> 02:17:02.078
<i>How do you solve a problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:02.889 --> 02:17:06.586
<i>How do you catch a cloud</i>
<i>And pin it down?</i>

02:17:07.561 --> 02:17:11.725
<i>How do you find a word</i>
<i>That means Maria?</i>

02:17:12.165 --> 02:17:13.154
<i>A flibbertigibbet</i>

02:17:13.400 --> 02:17:16.665
<i>A will-o'-the-wisp</i>
<i>A clown</i>

02:17:16.870 --> 02:17:21.432
<i>Many a thing you know</i>
<i>You'd like to tell her</i>

02:17:21.875 --> 02:17:25.902
<i>Many a thing she ought to understand</i>

02:17:26.613 --> 02:17:30.913
<i>But how do you make her stay</i>
<i>And listen to all you say?</i>

02:17:31.284 --> 02:17:35.220
<i>How do you keep a wave upon the sand?</i>

02:17:35.555 --> 02:17:40.549
<i>Oh, how do you solve</i>
<i>A problem like Maria?</i>

02:17:40.927 --> 02:17:47.560
<i>How do you hold a moonbeam</i>
<i>In your hand?</i>

02:19:53.660 --> 02:19:55.218
Herr Detweiler!

02:19:57.831 --> 02:20:00.493
- Heil Hitler.
- Oh, good afternoon, Herr Zeller.

02:20:00.734 --> 02:20:04.033
Perhaps you've not heard.
I am now the Gauleiter.

02:20:04.337 --> 02:20:05.861
Heil Hitler.

02:20:06.773 --> 02:20:07.933
Heil Hitler.

02:20:08.241 --> 02:20:10.505
I've come from
Captain von Trapp's house.

02:20:10.944 --> 02:20:14.539
The only one in the area
not flying the Third Reich flag...

02:20:14.781 --> 02:20:16.043
...since the Anschluss.

02:20:16.249 --> 02:20:18.410
- But we have dealt with that.
- I don't...

02:20:18.685 --> 02:20:21.620
The housekeeper told me
that I would find you here.

02:20:21.888 --> 02:20:23.583
The only thing she'd tell me.

02:20:24.090 --> 02:20:26.615
What kind of information
are you looking for?

02:20:26.893 --> 02:20:28.758
When will the captain return?

02:20:29.296 --> 02:20:33.232
Well, he's on his honeymoon trip.
He's not been in touch with us.

02:20:33.466 --> 02:20:38.301
Am I to believe he hasn't communicated
with his children in over a month?

02:20:38.572 --> 02:20:40.472
How many men do you know...

02:20:40.740 --> 02:20:44.039
...who communicate with their children
while honeymooning?

02:20:44.945 --> 02:20:48.642
Upon his return, he'll fill
his proper position in the new order.

02:20:48.949 --> 02:20:51.315
Naturally.
And may I congratulate you...

02:20:51.551 --> 02:20:56.215
...and your people in allowing the
festival to go on tonight as planned.

02:20:56.756 --> 02:21:00.214
Why should it not go on?
Nothing in Austria has changed.

02:21:00.460 --> 02:21:03.861
Singing and music will
show this to the world.

02:21:04.064 --> 02:21:05.759
Austria is the same.

02:21:06.633 --> 02:21:07.998
Heil Hitler.

02:21:10.170 --> 02:21:11.762
Heil Hitler.

02:21:13.440 --> 02:21:14.668
Come, let's go home.

02:21:14.908 --> 02:21:18.400
- Why was he so cross?
- Everybody's cross these days.

02:21:18.612 --> 02:21:21.979
Maybe the flag with the black spider
makes people nervous.

02:21:22.182 --> 02:21:25.117
- Will Father be in trouble?
- He doesn't have to be.

02:21:25.352 --> 02:21:28.082
The thing to do
is to get along with everybody.

02:21:28.321 --> 02:21:30.516
Remember that tonight at the concert.

02:21:30.757 --> 02:21:33.658
Are we really going to sing
before a lot of people?

02:21:33.860 --> 02:21:35.953
Look. The von Trapp Family Singers:

02:21:36.162 --> 02:21:40.758
Liesl, Friedrich, Louisa, Brigitta,
Kurt, Marta and Gretl.

02:21:40.967 --> 02:21:45.336
- Why am I always last?
- Because you are the most important.

02:21:46.039 --> 02:21:47.666
There we go.

02:21:53.546 --> 02:21:57.004
Are you sure Father will approve
of our singing in public?

02:21:57.217 --> 02:21:59.515
He'll be pleased and proud.

02:21:59.986 --> 02:22:02.454
- Liesl, do you think so?
- Don't you trust me?

02:22:02.656 --> 02:22:03.680
No.

02:22:03.890 --> 02:22:05.983
You're a very intelligent girl.

02:22:06.526 --> 02:22:08.687
Liesl. Liesl!

02:22:09.629 --> 02:22:10.823
Rolfe!

02:22:11.831 --> 02:22:13.856
I'm so glad to see you.
It's been su...

02:22:14.067 --> 02:22:15.159
Good afternoon.

02:22:15.568 --> 02:22:18.503
Give this to your father
as soon as he's home.

02:22:19.172 --> 02:22:21.037
- He's on his honeymoon.
- I know.

02:22:21.241 --> 02:22:24.574
- You do?
- We make it our business to know all.

02:22:25.312 --> 02:22:27.872
- Who's "we"?
- See that he gets it.

02:22:28.081 --> 02:22:30.413
- What is it?
- It's a telegram from Berlin.

02:22:31.251 --> 02:22:33.742
Don't you want to deliver it yourself?

02:22:34.220 --> 02:22:36.848
I'm occupied
with more important matters.

02:22:37.057 --> 02:22:39.548
And your father had better be too.

02:22:39.826 --> 02:22:41.316
But, Rolfe!

02:23:04.417 --> 02:23:06.078
Father!

02:23:06.353 --> 02:23:09.015
- We didn't expect you so soon.
- Hello, hello!

02:23:09.255 --> 02:23:12.053
We didn't expect you home
until next week!

02:23:12.258 --> 02:23:17.696
- Did you bring souvenirs from Paris?
- Hello! How are you?

02:23:18.798 --> 02:23:20.095
Why didn't you call us?

02:23:20.300 --> 02:23:22.234
We couldn't get through.

02:23:22.535 --> 02:23:24.469
I had nothing to do with that.

02:23:24.738 --> 02:23:26.763
We came back as fast as we could.

02:23:27.073 --> 02:23:29.234
Well, well, well! We missed you!

02:23:29.476 --> 02:23:31.910
- We missed you!
- We missed kissing you.

02:23:32.112 --> 02:23:34.945
We missed all the noise
in the morning.

02:23:35.215 --> 02:23:39.413
- Mostly, we missed hearing you sing.
- Oh, you came back just in time.

02:23:39.619 --> 02:23:41.382
Look, Fräulein Maria...

02:23:41.588 --> 02:23:43.215
I mean Mother.

02:23:43.623 --> 02:23:46.114
We're going to sing
in the festival tonight.

02:23:46.326 --> 02:23:48.453
We've been having a lovely time!

02:23:48.728 --> 02:23:50.787
We've been rehearsing all...

02:23:52.298 --> 02:23:54.630
Surprise! Surprise!

02:23:55.301 --> 02:23:57.792
Surprises for you on the terrace.

02:24:00.840 --> 02:24:02.239
We'll talk about this.

02:24:02.442 --> 02:24:06.742
I would've told you but you were away.
I had to make a last-minute decision.

02:24:07.013 --> 02:24:09.504
I was fortunate to enter them at all.

02:24:09.749 --> 02:24:14.482
They'll be the talk of the festival.
Imagine, seven children in one family!

02:24:14.687 --> 02:24:16.314
Max!

02:24:16.923 --> 02:24:19.756
Somehow I recall having made it
quite clear to you...

02:24:20.026 --> 02:24:22.688
...how I feel about my family
singing in public!

02:24:22.962 --> 02:24:24.657
The committee was enchanted.

02:24:24.864 --> 02:24:28.027
- What did they say?
- I have never heard such enthusiasm.

02:24:28.301 --> 02:24:32.601
- Don't you think just this once...?
- Absolutely out of the question.

02:24:32.839 --> 02:24:36.969
- Georg, this is for Austria.
- For Austria?

02:24:37.343 --> 02:24:40.608
- There is no Austria!
- But the Anschluss was peaceful.

02:24:40.847 --> 02:24:44.305
- Let's at least be grateful for that.
- Grateful?

02:24:46.186 --> 02:24:47.847
You know, Max...

02:24:48.721 --> 02:24:51.986
...sometimes I don't believe
I know you.

02:24:54.661 --> 02:24:56.026
Father, I forgot.

02:24:56.863 --> 02:24:58.455
This is for you.

02:25:08.241 --> 02:25:12.234
Maria, he has got to at least pretend
to work with these people.

02:25:12.512 --> 02:25:14.036
You must convince him.

02:25:14.247 --> 02:25:17.011
Max, I can't ask him
to be less than he is.

02:25:17.250 --> 02:25:20.549
Then I'll talk to him.
If the children don't sing, well...

02:25:20.820 --> 02:25:23.050
...it will be a reflection
on Austria.

02:25:23.857 --> 02:25:27.224
Oh, I know.
It wouldn't do me any good either.

02:25:32.398 --> 02:25:35.060
Mother? That sounds so nice.

02:25:35.335 --> 02:25:38.065
- I like calling you "Mother."
- I like hearing it.

02:25:38.271 --> 02:25:42.002
You love Father very much.
I can tell you do.

02:25:42.208 --> 02:25:43.004
Very much.

02:25:43.276 --> 02:25:46.575
Mother, what do you do when you
think you love someone?

02:25:47.280 --> 02:25:52.582
I mean, when you stop loving someone
or he stops loving you?

02:25:55.188 --> 02:25:57.247
Well, you cry a little.

02:25:57.690 --> 02:25:59.783
Then you wait for the sun to come out.

02:26:00.093 --> 02:26:01.424
It always does.

02:26:01.694 --> 02:26:05.255
There are so many things I think
I should know but I don't.

02:26:05.465 --> 02:26:07.433
- I really don't.
- How can you?

02:26:07.700 --> 02:26:09.895
Sometimes I feel the world is ending.

02:26:10.136 --> 02:26:13.367
- Then you feel it's just beginning?
- Yes!

02:26:13.573 --> 02:26:17.805
It was that way with me. And for you
it will be just as wonderful.

02:26:18.478 --> 02:26:20.378
Do you really think so?

02:26:21.281 --> 02:26:25.217
<i>When you're 16 going on 17</i>

02:26:25.485 --> 02:26:29.080
<i>Waiting for life to start</i>

02:26:29.756 --> 02:26:33.590
<i>Somebody kind</i>
<i>Who touches your mind</i>

02:26:33.826 --> 02:26:38.126
<i>Will suddenly touch your heart</i>

02:26:38.565 --> 02:26:40.260
<i>When that happens</i>

02:26:40.733 --> 02:26:42.667
<i>After it happens</i>

02:26:42.902 --> 02:26:46.770
<i>Nothing is quite the same</i>

02:26:47.006 --> 02:26:48.564
<i>Somehow I know</i>

02:26:48.841 --> 02:26:50.968
<i>I'll jump up and go</i>

02:26:51.177 --> 02:26:55.477
<i>If ever he calls my name</i>

02:26:55.748 --> 02:26:59.650
<i>Gone are your old ideas of life</i>

02:26:59.919 --> 02:27:04.117
<i>The old ideas grow dim</i>

02:27:04.357 --> 02:27:08.760
<i>Lo and behold</i>
<i>You're someone's wife</i>

02:27:09.696 --> 02:27:15.692
<i>And you belong to him</i>

02:27:16.002 --> 02:27:20.302
<i>You may think this kind of adventure</i>

02:27:20.506 --> 02:27:24.374
<i>Never may come to you</i>

02:27:25.478 --> 02:27:30.848
<i>Darling, 16 going on 17</i>

02:27:31.684 --> 02:27:35.814
<i>Wait a year...</i>

02:27:36.623 --> 02:27:41.856
<i>- I'll wait a year</i>
<i>...or two</i>

02:27:42.295 --> 02:27:49.633
<i>Just wait a year...</i>

02:27:50.503 --> 02:27:59.138
<i>...or two</i>

02:28:01.547 --> 02:28:03.139
Liesl.

02:28:19.599 --> 02:28:20.930
What is it?

02:28:21.868 --> 02:28:23.233
Berlin.

02:28:23.703 --> 02:28:25.568
They've offered me a commission.

02:28:25.838 --> 02:28:28.363
I've been requested
to accept immediately...

02:28:28.608 --> 02:28:32.601
...and report to their naval base
at Bremerhaven tomorrow.

02:28:33.212 --> 02:28:37.205
I knew this would happen.
I didn't think it would be so soon.

02:28:37.450 --> 02:28:40.942
To refuse them would be fatal
for all of us.

02:28:42.188 --> 02:28:45.954
And joining them would be unthinkable.

02:28:52.131 --> 02:28:53.894
Get the children all together.

02:28:54.233 --> 02:28:57.430
Don't say anything to worry them.
Just get them ready.

02:28:58.404 --> 02:29:00.770
We've got to get out of Austria...

02:29:02.442 --> 02:29:04.103
...and this house...

02:29:06.446 --> 02:29:07.879
...tonight.

02:29:51.791 --> 02:29:54.191
This strains my back
and breaks my heart...

02:29:54.460 --> 02:29:57.293
...when I think of the children
missing the festival.

02:29:57.597 --> 02:30:00.259
By your announcement
we'll be over the border.

02:30:00.500 --> 02:30:02.934
Do you appreciate
the sacrifice I'm making?

02:30:03.136 --> 02:30:04.433
You have no choice.

02:30:04.670 --> 02:30:07.503
I know. That's why I'm making it.

02:30:08.207 --> 02:30:10.334
Why doesn't Father turn the motor on?

02:30:10.543 --> 02:30:13.979
Because he doesn't want anyone
to hear us.

02:30:17.617 --> 02:30:20.051
What will Frau Schmidt and Franz say?

02:30:20.319 --> 02:30:23.846
They'll be able to answer honestly
they didn't know anything.

02:30:24.056 --> 02:30:28.288
- Will we be coming back here?
- Someday, Liesl. I do hope someday.

02:30:28.528 --> 02:30:33.465
Are Father and Uncle Max going to push
the car all the way to Switzerland?

02:31:00.259 --> 02:31:02.659
Something wrong
with your car, captain?

02:31:02.995 --> 02:31:05.259
Yes, we couldn't get it started.

02:31:09.035 --> 02:31:10.263
Karl.

02:31:12.238 --> 02:31:15.730
Fix Captain von Trapp's car
so that it will start.

02:31:38.931 --> 02:31:40.728
Excellent, Karl.

02:31:44.103 --> 02:31:47.266
I've not asked you where you
and your family are going.

02:31:47.773 --> 02:31:49.900
Nor have you asked me why I'm here.

02:31:50.109 --> 02:31:53.875
Apparently we both suffer
from a deplorable lack of curiosity.

02:31:54.747 --> 02:31:57.215
You never answered the telegram...

02:31:57.450 --> 02:32:00.749
...from the Admiral of the Navy
of the Third Reich.

02:32:00.987 --> 02:32:03.455
I was under the impression,
Herr Zeller...

02:32:03.723 --> 02:32:07.215
...that the contents of telegrams
in Austria are private!

02:32:07.927 --> 02:32:11.454
At least, the Austria I know.

02:32:12.598 --> 02:32:14.225
I have my orders...

02:32:14.467 --> 02:32:16.628
...to take you
to Bremerhaven tonight...

02:32:16.903 --> 02:32:19.098
...where you will accept
your commission.

02:32:20.239 --> 02:32:25.677
I'm afraid that's going to be
quite impossible.

02:32:26.279 --> 02:32:28.008
You see, we...

02:32:28.581 --> 02:32:31.414
...all of us, the entire family,
will be...

02:32:32.485 --> 02:32:34.510
...singing in the festival tonight.

02:32:34.820 --> 02:32:37.288
As a matter of fact, we're going now.

02:32:37.924 --> 02:32:40.791
We couldn't possibly
let them down now.

02:32:40.993 --> 02:32:43.962
- I just hope we're not too late.
- Yes.

02:32:44.196 --> 02:32:47.097
You ask me to believe that you,
Captain von Trapp...

02:32:47.333 --> 02:32:48.800
...are singing in a concert?

02:32:49.201 --> 02:32:53.331
Believe me, it will be a performance
beyond anything even I've dreamt of.

02:32:53.706 --> 02:32:58.336
Like you, Herr Zeller,
I, too, am a man of hidden talents.

02:32:59.045 --> 02:33:00.376
Yes.

02:33:00.646 --> 02:33:03.137
Here, program.

02:33:08.154 --> 02:33:10.486
It says only the names
of the children.

02:33:10.723 --> 02:33:13.988
It says
the von Trapp Family Singers...

02:33:14.226 --> 02:33:17.286
...and I am the head of
the von Trapp family, am I not?

02:33:19.565 --> 02:33:23.365
And these travel clothes
that you're all wearing?

02:33:24.203 --> 02:33:25.727
Our costumes, naturally.

02:33:26.005 --> 02:33:29.406
This night air is not good
for the children's voices.

02:33:35.648 --> 02:33:39.175
Well, a slight delay in my orders
will not be serious.

02:33:40.386 --> 02:33:41.910
Therefore...

02:33:42.755 --> 02:33:44.382
...you will sing.

02:33:45.324 --> 02:33:47.315
You will all sing.

02:33:47.693 --> 02:33:50.218
But only because that's what I want.

02:33:51.163 --> 02:33:54.599
It will demonstrate that nothing
in Austria has changed.

02:33:55.334 --> 02:33:57.529
And when you have finished singing...

02:33:57.837 --> 02:34:01.000
...you, Captain von Trapp, will be
taken to Bremerhaven.

02:34:02.274 --> 02:34:05.004
Now, if you will all get
into your car...

02:34:05.244 --> 02:34:09.078
...we will escort the von Trapp Family
Singers to the festival.

02:34:09.949 --> 02:34:12.110
No escort will be necessary.

02:34:12.351 --> 02:34:14.842
Necessary? A pleasure, captain.

02:34:15.755 --> 02:34:19.623
After all, we would not want you
to get lost in the crowds.

02:34:20.860 --> 02:34:22.350
Would we?

02:34:23.029 --> 02:34:24.189
No.

02:34:40.413 --> 02:34:43.576
<i>Sew, a needle pulling thread</i>

02:34:43.783 --> 02:34:46.980
<i>La, a note to follow sew</i>

02:34:47.253 --> 02:34:50.711
<i>Tea, a drink with jam and bread</i>

02:34:50.923 --> 02:34:54.723
<i>A drink with jam and bread</i>

02:35:04.303 --> 02:35:06.464
<i>Tea with jam</i>
<i>Jam and bread</i>

02:35:12.344 --> 02:35:15.677
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- A, B, C</i>

02:35:15.915 --> 02:35:19.146
<i>- With jam</i>
<i>- Do-re-mi</i>

02:35:19.351 --> 02:35:22.946
<i>Tea with jam and bread</i>

02:35:23.189 --> 02:35:24.520
<i>With jam and bread</i>

02:35:24.790 --> 02:35:26.314
<i>With jam</i>
<i>With jam...</i>

02:35:26.525 --> 02:35:35.331
<i>...and bread</i>

02:35:57.323 --> 02:36:00.451
My fellow Austrians...

02:36:01.727 --> 02:36:06.289
...I shall not be seeing you again,
perhaps for a very long time.

02:36:07.700 --> 02:36:09.361
I would like to sing for you now...

02:36:10.970 --> 02:36:12.528
...a love song.

02:36:14.507 --> 02:36:16.702
I know you share this love.

02:36:18.010 --> 02:36:21.707
I pray that you will never let it die.

02:36:34.493 --> 02:36:38.020
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:38.230 --> 02:36:41.427
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:36:41.700 --> 02:36:47.434
<i>Every morning you greet me</i>

02:36:47.840 --> 02:36:50.900
<i>Small and white</i>

02:36:51.177 --> 02:36:53.941
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:36:54.513 --> 02:36:59.610
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:00.386 --> 02:37:02.411
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:02.688 --> 02:37:06.283
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:37:06.525 --> 02:37:12.191
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:37:13.699 --> 02:37:16.190
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:16.435 --> 02:37:19.063
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:19.271 --> 02:37:25.267
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:37:29.782 --> 02:37:32.876
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:37:33.118 --> 02:37:34.449
<i>Edel...</i>

02:37:41.827 --> 02:37:44.921
<i>Small and white</i>

02:37:45.130 --> 02:37:47.997
<i>Clean and bright</i>

02:37:48.234 --> 02:37:53.570
<i>You look happy to meet me</i>

02:37:54.406 --> 02:37:56.374
<i>Blossom of snow</i>

02:37:56.575 --> 02:37:59.976
<i>May you bloom and grow</i>

02:38:00.646 --> 02:38:06.642
<i>Bloom and grow forever</i>

02:38:07.119 --> 02:38:10.020
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:10.322 --> 02:38:13.086
<i>Edelweiss</i>

02:38:13.692 --> 02:38:21.929
<i>Bless my homeland forever</i>

02:38:39.652 --> 02:38:41.210
I think it'll work.

02:38:41.954 --> 02:38:43.717
I shall miss all of you.

02:38:44.223 --> 02:38:46.657
I shall miss the money
I could have made with you.

02:38:50.062 --> 02:38:51.620
Thank you, ladies and gentlemen.

02:38:52.364 --> 02:38:55.026
The competition has come
to its conclusion...

02:38:55.301 --> 02:38:58.395
...except, we don't know
yet what that conclusion will be.

02:38:59.371 --> 02:39:01.896
And while the judges
arrive at their decision...

02:39:02.174 --> 02:39:05.200
...I have been given permission
to offer you an encore.

02:39:05.477 --> 02:39:08.674
This will be the last opportunity
the von Trapps will have...

02:39:08.914 --> 02:39:11.314
...of singing together
for a long, long time.

02:39:12.384 --> 02:39:16.377
Even now, officials are waiting
in this auditorium...

02:39:16.655 --> 02:39:19.385
...to escort Captain von Trapp
to his new command...

02:39:19.591 --> 02:39:23.152
...in the naval forces
of the Third Reich.

02:39:27.833 --> 02:39:32.361
And so, ladies and gentlemen,
the family von Trapp again...

02:39:33.005 --> 02:39:35.269
...to bid you farewell.

02:39:42.514 --> 02:39:46.109
<i>There's a sad sort of clanging</i>
<i>From the clock in the hall</i>

02:39:46.385 --> 02:39:49.718
<i>And the bells in the steeple too</i>

02:39:50.222 --> 02:39:54.090
<i>And up in the nursery</i>
<i>An absurd little bird</i>

02:39:54.293 --> 02:39:56.727
<i>Is popping out to say "coo-coo"</i>

02:39:56.929 --> 02:39:58.590
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:39:58.864 --> 02:39:59.853
<i>Coo-coo</i>

02:40:00.132 --> 02:40:01.724
<i>Regretfully they tell us</i>

02:40:01.934 --> 02:40:03.731
<i>But firmly they compel us</i>

02:40:03.969 --> 02:40:06.733
<i>To say goodbye</i>

02:40:06.939 --> 02:40:12.104
<i>To you</i>

02:40:15.080 --> 02:40:18.607
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, good night</i>

02:40:18.884 --> 02:40:22.615
<i>We hate to go</i>
<i>And miss this pretty sight</i>

02:40:28.794 --> 02:40:32.389
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, adieu</i>

02:40:32.598 --> 02:40:36.261
<i>Adieu, adieu</i>
<i>To you and you and you</i>

02:40:42.574 --> 02:40:46.169
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:40:46.412 --> 02:40:48.004
<i>We flit, we float</i>

02:40:48.280 --> 02:40:49.941
<i>We fleetly flee, we fly</i>

02:40:56.321 --> 02:41:00.121
<i>So long, farewell</i>
<i>Auf Wiedersehen, goodbye</i>

02:41:00.325 --> 02:41:03.692
<i>The sun has gone to bed</i>
<i>And so must I</i>

02:41:03.962 --> 02:41:07.762
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:08.000 --> 02:41:13.700
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:13.939 --> 02:41:19.138
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:19.378 --> 02:41:26.546
<i>Goodbye</i>

02:41:58.350 --> 02:42:02.480
Ladies and gentlemen, I have here the
decision of our distinguished judges.

02:42:02.688 --> 02:42:05.248
We will start with the award
for third prize.

02:42:05.891 --> 02:42:08.223
For this honor,
the judges have named...

02:42:08.494 --> 02:42:13.090
...the first soloist of the choir
of St. Agatha's Church in Murback.

02:42:13.365 --> 02:42:15.595
Fräulein Schweiger.

02:42:52.538 --> 02:42:56.474
Second prize
to The Toby Reiser Quintet.

02:43:24.436 --> 02:43:28.600
And the first prize,
the highest honor in all Austria...

02:43:28.840 --> 02:43:31.934
...the von Trapp Family Singers.

02:43:44.323 --> 02:43:45.984
The family von Trapp.

02:44:00.606 --> 02:44:01.664
They're gone!

02:44:20.359 --> 02:44:21.792
Come with me.

02:44:25.631 --> 02:44:27.622
Quickly, quickly.

02:44:28.533 --> 02:44:30.728
I have a place you can hide.

02:44:31.470 --> 02:44:34.735
Slowly, slowly.

02:44:45.717 --> 02:44:47.412
Open this gate.

02:44:48.553 --> 02:44:50.145
Good evening.

02:44:52.658 --> 02:44:54.091
Hurry up, woman.

02:45:13.945 --> 02:45:15.207
Two men in there.

02:45:15.414 --> 02:45:17.279
Six of you cover the yard.

02:45:17.516 --> 02:45:19.746
You two, cover the corridor.

02:45:34.232 --> 02:45:37.793
Reverend Mother, we didn't realize
we put the abbey in this danger.

02:45:38.070 --> 02:45:40.595
No, Maria, it was right for you
to come here.

02:45:40.806 --> 02:45:42.706
We thought we might borrow
your car.

02:45:42.908 --> 02:45:44.808
I'm afraid our car will do you
no good now.

02:45:45.410 --> 02:45:47.071
I've been listening to the wires.

02:45:47.279 --> 02:45:49.804
The borders have just been closed.

02:45:55.654 --> 02:45:57.952
All right,
if the borders are closed...

02:45:59.257 --> 02:46:02.556
...then we'll drive up into the hills
and go over the mountains on foot.

02:46:03.161 --> 02:46:05.152
- The children...
- We'll help them.

02:46:05.430 --> 02:46:07.591
We can do it without help, Father.

02:46:08.633 --> 02:46:09.998
Maria.

02:46:10.736 --> 02:46:13.330
You will not be alone.
Remember:

02:46:13.572 --> 02:46:16.666
"I will lift up mine eyes unto
the hills from whence cometh my help."

02:46:17.642 --> 02:46:18.734
Yes, Mother.

02:46:20.112 --> 02:46:22.273
- I'm scared.
- Me too.

02:46:34.359 --> 02:46:35.519
God be with you.

02:46:42.467 --> 02:46:44.025
- Mother.
- Yes?

02:46:44.269 --> 02:46:47.466
Would it help if we sang
about our favorite things?

02:46:47.706 --> 02:46:50.698
No, darling.
This is one time it would not help.

02:46:50.976 --> 02:46:54.173
You must be very quiet.
Hold tight to me.

02:49:08.847 --> 02:49:10.075
Let's try the roof.

02:50:06.338 --> 02:50:08.568
Rolfe, please.

02:50:13.678 --> 02:50:15.168
No, wait.

02:50:24.990 --> 02:50:26.321
Maria.

02:50:27.392 --> 02:50:28.825
Children.

02:50:32.864 --> 02:50:35.890
It's you we want, not them.

02:50:36.267 --> 02:50:37.996
Put that down.

02:50:39.070 --> 02:50:42.369
Not another move,
or I'll shoot.

02:50:44.075 --> 02:50:46.100
You're only a boy.

02:50:49.114 --> 02:50:52.777
- You don't really belong to them.
- Stay where you are.

02:50:54.552 --> 02:50:56.543
Come away with us.

02:50:57.789 --> 02:50:58.949
Before it's too late.

02:50:59.557 --> 02:51:01.889
Not another step.
I'll kill you.

02:51:04.195 --> 02:51:07.528
- You give that to me, Rolfe.
- Did you hear me?

02:51:08.533 --> 02:51:10.091
I'll kill you.

02:51:11.970 --> 02:51:13.437
Rolfe.

02:51:31.823 --> 02:51:33.154
You'll never be one of them.

02:51:35.927 --> 02:51:37.622
Lieutenant!

02:51:37.896 --> 02:51:39.022
They're here!

02:51:39.230 --> 02:51:40.788
They're here, lieutenant!

02:52:22.107 --> 02:52:23.768
Reverend Mother.

02:52:25.043 --> 02:52:26.874
I have sinned.

02:52:28.046 --> 02:52:30.207
I too, Reverend Mother.

02:52:31.850 --> 02:52:34.182
What is this sin, my children?

